    This experiment tests the hypothesis that a series of small, iterative adjustments in the latent space will allow batch distributions to merge more naturally than the single, rigid translation I attempted previously (ID 1078). A successful outcome would manifest as an improved local mixing score (`iLISI`) while maintaining the strong global correction (`PCR`) observed in the single-step method.


