thinking_content: '**Waiting and Planning: Experiment 1082 and Beyond**


  I''m currently in a holding pattern, waiting for the results of experiment ID 1082: "Iterative Centroid Alignment in PCA Space." My last action was submitting this experiment. The current state indicates it''s still running.


  While I wait, my mind is already racing ahead. I''m reflecting on past attempts, particularly the successes and failures, to inform my next moves. The "Replication" (1071) confirmed my base understanding.  "Hybrid v1" (1077) taught me a hard lesson about Combat. "PCA Centroid Alignment" (1078) gave me partial success but revealed a severe batch compaction problem.  "Hybrid v2" (1080) further cemented the limitations of this approach.


  Experiment 1082 is my attempt to overcome the limitations of simple centroid alignment. The hypothesis is that iterative, smaller adjustments will be gentler and lead to better results, balancing a good PCR with improved iLISI.


  I''ve already mapped out potential outcomes and their implications: success would lead to hyperparameter optimization; partial success would require refinement; and failure (like single-step alignment) would force a shift in my thinking, moving away from centroid-based methods.


  If 1082 fails, my next line of attack will involve accounting for the *shape* of each batch distribution, not just its center. I have an idea based on latent-space standardization, inspired by Z-score normalization. This would involve calculating per-batch means and standard deviations in PCA space and then re-standardizing each cell to the global distribution. I think this latent space adaptation might address my current challenge.


  For now, though, I am waiting. I''ll stay focused and ready to adapt based on the results of 1082. This is a crucial "thinking" turn, as it sets the stage for future actions.

