    \  ASW_batch: 0.816001  ASW_label: 0.533131  ARI: 0.578861  NMI: 0.680886\n  Graph_conn: 0.879011  kBET: 0.744637  iLISI: 0.020802  cLISI: 0.997019\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.357385\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1100\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The code was fixed with a simple one-line import addition and achieved a score of **0.6173753087985372**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission used `pd.get_dummies()` on line 20 to perform one-hot encoding of batch labels, but never imported the pandas library. This resulted in a `NameError: name 'pd' is not defined` when the code attempted to execute.\n\nThe error occurred at:\n```python\nbatch_dummies = pd.get_dummies(batch_dummies['batch'], drop_first=True).values\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing pandas import at the top of the file:\n```python\nimport pandas as pd  # FIXED: Added missing pandas import\n```\n\nThis was the only change required. The fix was implemented in `submissions/submission_v2.py`.\n\
    \n## Verification\nThe fixed code was automatically evaluated by the system and:\n- Executed without any errors\n- Completed all processing stages (PCA, batch PC identification, standardization with targeted overscaling)\n- Generated valid output in the expected AnnData format\n- Achieved a batch integration score of 0.6173753087985372\n\n## Technical Details\nThe algorithm implements \"Standardization with Targeted Variance Overscaling\", which:\n1. Performs PCA on normalized and log-transformed data\n2. Identifies principal components associated with batch effects using linear regression (R² > 0.1)\n3. Applies variance overscaling (factor of 1.2) specifically to batch-associated PCs\n4. Performs per-batch standardization followed by global rescaling\n5. Returns corrected embeddings in PCA space\n\nThe missing import was a simple oversight in an otherwise well-structured implementation.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies\
    \ on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nStandardization with Targeted Variance Overscaling\n\nThis method improves upon 'Latent Space Standardization' by applying variance\noverscaling only to the principal components most associated with the batch effect.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd  # FIXED: Added missing pandas import\nfrom sklearn.linear_model import LinearRegression\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Standardization with Targeted Overscaling: Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Parameters ---\n    overscale_factor = 1.2 # A slightly more aggressive factor\n    n_pcs = 50\n    # Identify PCs where R-squared with batch is > 0.1\n    batch_pc_r2_threshold = 0.1\n\n    # === STAGE 1: Initial PCA and Batch PC Identification ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] PCA and identifying batch-associated\
    \ PCs...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n    # One-hot encode batch labels for regression\n    batch_dummies = sc.get.obs_df(adata, keys=['batch'])\n    batch_dummies = pd.get_dummies(batch_dummies['batch'], drop_first=True).values\n\n    batch_assoc_pcs = []\n    for i in range(X_pca.shape[1]):\n        pc_vector = X_pca[:, i].reshape(-1, 1)\n        model = LinearRegression().fit(batch_dummies, pc_vector)\n        r2 = model.score(batch_dummies, pc_vector)\n        if r2 > batch_pc_r2_threshold:\n            batch_assoc_pcs.append(i)\n\n    print(f\"  [Stage 1] Identified {len(batch_assoc_pcs)} batch-associated PCs: {batch_assoc_pcs}\")\n\n    # === STAGE 2: Standardization with Targeted Overscaling ===\n    print(f\"  [Stage 2] Performing standardization with targeted overscaling...\")\n\
    \    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n    unique_batches = batch_labels.unique()\n    X_pca_corrected = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n\n    for pc_idx in range(X_pca.shape[1]):\n        pc_vector = X_pca[:, pc_idx]\n        global_mean, global_std = pc_vector.mean(), pc_vector.std()\n\n        # Determine the scaling factor for this PC\n        current_scale_factor = overscale_factor if pc_idx in batch_assoc_pcs else 1.0\n\n        for batch in unique_batches:\n            batch_mask = (batch_labels == batch).values\n            if np.any(batch_mask):\n                batch_pc = pc_vector[batch_mask]\n                batch_mean, batch_std = batch_pc.mean(), batch_pc.std()\n                if batch_std < 1e-8: batch_std = 1.0\n\n                standardized = (batch_pc - batch_mean) / batch_std\n                rescaled = standardized * (global_std * current_scale_factor) + global_mean\n                X_pca_corrected[batch_mask, pc_idx] = rescaled\n\n    print(\"  [Stage 2] Standardization\
    \ complete.\")\n\n    # === STAGE 3: Create Output ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_pca_corrected.astype(np.float32)},\n        uns={'method_id': 'pca_targeted_overscale'}\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Targeted Overscaling complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nStandardization with Targeted Overscaling: Starting...\n  [Stage 1] PCA and identifying batch-associated PCs...\n  [Stage 1] Identified 7 batch-associated PCs: [0, 3, 5, 6, 9, 15, 21]\n  [Stage 2] Performing standardization with targeted overscaling...\n  [Stage 2] Standardization complete.\n✓ Targeted Overscaling complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph:\
    \ False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7800ada4-6c84-4484-9f09-6475d8c342cb/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7800ada4-6c84-4484-9f09-6475d8c342cb\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1100 | 1 | Standardization with Targeted Variance Overscaling | Axiom I | 716 | 0.6174\
    \ | 0.579 | 0.627 | 0.210 | 0.409 | 0.877 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.021 | 0.780 |\n| 1098 | 1 | Canonical Correlation Analysis (CCA) based Correction | Axiom I | 714 | 0.5005 | 0.683 | 0.528 | 0.220 | 0.311 | 0.880 | 0.696 | 0.009 | 0.988 | 0.063 | 0.628 |\n| 1095 | 1 | Standardization with Variance Overscaling (1.1x) | Axiom I | 712 | 0.6174 | 0.587 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.780 |\n| 1092 | 1 | MNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing | Axiom I | 710 | 0.5769 | 0.687 | 0.561 | 0.236 | 0.375 | 0.874 | 0.724 | 0.234 | 0.991 | 0.173 | 0.915 |\n| 1091 | 1 | Hybrid v4: Latent Standardization + MNN Residual Correction | Axiom I | 709 | 0.4697 | 0.411 | 0.538 | 0.216 | 0.368 | 0.830 | 0.629 | 0.000 | 0.990 | 0.000 | 0.716 |\n| 1089 | 1 | MNN-based Correction in Latent Space | Axiom I | 707 | 0.5728 | 0.757 | 0.450 | 0.224 | 0.366 | 0.860 | 0.702 | 0.277 | 0.993 | 0.277 | 0.823 |\n| 1087 | 1 | Hybrid v3: Latent Standardization + BBKNN Graph |\
    \ Axiom I | 706 | 0.1759 | 0.117 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.210 | 0.431 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1085 | 1 | Latent Space Standardization (Mean and Variance Correction) | Axiom I | 705 | 0.6173 | 0.589 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.776 |\n| 1082 | 1 | Iterative Centroid Alignment in PCA Space | Axiom I | 703 | 0.5787 | 0.462 | 0.624 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.888 | 0.671 | 0.979 | 0.991 | 0.006 | 0.599 |\n| 1080 | 1 | Hybrid v2: PCA Centroid Alignment + BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 702 | 0.1760 | 0.117 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.199 | 0.444 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation &\
