- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 720\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 99,946 / 300,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 30 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Graph Correction with a Penalized Distance Metric' (ID: 1102) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.2939888733577063\n**ASW_batch:** 0.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.415\n**NMI:** 0.635\n**Graph_conn:** 0.899\n**kBET:** 0.000\n**iLISI:** 0.000\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.000\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.415  NMI: 0.635\n  Graph_conn: 0.899  kBET: 0.000  iLISI: 0.000  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.000\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: nan  ASW_label: nan  ARI: 0.414844  NMI: 0.635184\n  Graph_conn: 0.900703  kBET: nan  iLISI: 0.000000  cLISI: 0.997347\n  PCR: nan  Cell_cycle: 0.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1102\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in a single attempt. The submission now runs without crashing and achieved a score of 0.2939.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to create a boolean comparison matrix using NumPy broadcasting on pandas Categorical arrays:\n\n```python\nbatch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\nis_diff_batch = batch_labels[:, np.newaxis] != batch_labels[np.newaxis, :]\n```\n\nThe error occurred because:\n- `adata.obs['batch'].values` returns a pandas Categorical array\n- Pandas Categorical arrays have strict length-matching requirements for comparison operations\n- When using broadcasting with `np.newaxis`, pandas raises a `ValueError: Lengths must match` error\n- NumPy broadcasting doesn't work directly on pandas categorical\
    \ types\n\n## Fix Applied\nConverted the pandas Categorical array to a pure NumPy array before applying broadcasting:\n\n```python\nbatch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\nbatch_labels_array = np.asarray(batch_labels)  # Convert to numpy array\nis_diff_batch = batch_labels_array[:, np.newaxis] != batch_labels_array[np.newaxis, :]\n```\n\nThis simple conversion allows NumPy's broadcasting mechanism to work correctly, creating the desired boolean matrix where `M[i, j]` is `True` if cell `i` and cell `j` are from different batches.\n\n## Result\n- **Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Status**: Running successfully\n- **Score**: 0.2939888733577063\n- **Evaluation ID**: 1102\n\nThe algorithm's approach (penalized distance metric for k-NN graph construction) is sound. The fix only addressed a type compatibility issue between pandas and NumPy.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them\
    \ manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nGraph Correction with a Penalized Distance Metric\n\nThis method builds a k-NN graph using a custom distance metric that\npenalizes connections between different batches.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import lil_matrix\nfrom sklearn.metrics import pairwise_distances\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Graph Correction with Penalized Distance: Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Parameters ---\n    n_neighbors = 15\n    batch_penalty = 1.0 # Additive penalty for cross-batch distances\n\n    # === STAGE 1: Standard Preprocessing and PCA ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] Normalizing and computing PCA...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    n_pcs = 50\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n \
    \   X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n    n_cells = adata.n_obs\n\n    # === STAGE 2: Calculate Penalized Distance Matrix ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2] Calculating penalized distance matrix...\")\n\n    # Calculate standard Euclidean distances\n    dist_matrix = pairwise_distances(X_pca, metric='euclidean')\n\n    # Create a penalty matrix\n    # FIX: Convert pandas Series/Categorical to numpy array first\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    batch_labels_array = np.asarray(batch_labels)\n\n    # This creates a matrix where M[i, j] is 1 if batches are different, 0 otherwise\n    is_diff_batch = batch_labels_array[:, np.newaxis] != batch_labels_array[np.newaxis, :]\n    penalty_matrix = is_diff_batch.astype(np.float32) * batch_penalty\n\n    # Add the penalty to the distance matrix\n    penalized_dist_matrix = dist_matrix + penalty_matrix\n\n    print(f\"  [Stage 2] Penalty of {batch_penalty} applied to cross-batch connections.\")\n\n    # === STAGE 3: Find Neighbors and Construct\
    \ Graph ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 3] Finding k-NN and constructing graph...\")\n\n    # Find the k+1 nearest neighbors for each cell (including self)\n    # We use argpartition for efficiency as we don't need the full sorted list\n    neighbor_indices = np.argpartition(penalized_dist_matrix, kth=n_neighbors + 1, axis=1)[:, :n_neighbors + 1]\n\n    # Create sparse matrices for graph\n    distances_out = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n    connectivities_out = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for i in range(n_cells):\n        # Exclude self from neighbors\n        neighbors = neighbor_indices[i, neighbor_indices[i] != i]\n\n        # Get the original (unpenalized) distances to these neighbors\n        dists = dist_matrix[i, neighbors]\n\n        distances_out[i, neighbors] = dists\n        # Simple connectivity: 1 for connected, 0 otherwise\n        connectivities_out[i, neighbors] = 1\n\n    # Symmetrize matrices\n    distances_out = distances_out.tocsr().maximum(distances_out.T)\n\
    \    connectivities_out = connectivities_out.tocsr().maximum(connectivities_out.T)\n\n    print(\"  [Stage 3] Graph construction complete.\")\n\n    # === STAGE 4: Create Output ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsp={\n            'connectivities': connectivities_out,\n            'distances': distances_out,\n        },\n        uns={'method_id': 'penalized_distance_knn'}\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Penalized Distance Graph complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nGraph Correction with Penalized Distance: Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Normalizing and computing PCA...\n  [Stage 2] Calculating penalized distance matrix...\n  [Stage 2] Penalty of 1.0 applied to cross-batch\
    \ connections.\n  [Stage 3] Finding k-NN and constructing graph...\n  [Stage 3] Graph construction complete.\n✓ Penalized Distance Graph complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: False\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/85047355-4106-4a5a-8de5-cdecc1bd3da2/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 85047355-4106-4a5a-8de5-cdecc1bd3da2\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research\
    \ Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1102 | 1 | Graph Correction with a Penalized Distance Metric | Axiom I | 718 | 0.2940 | 0.415 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.899 | 0.635 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1100 | 1 | Standardization with Targeted Variance Overscaling | Axiom I | 716 | 0.6174 | 0.579 | 0.627 | 0.210 | 0.409 | 0.877 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.021 | 0.780 |\n| 1098 | 1 | Canonical Correlation Analysis (CCA) based Correction | Axiom I | 714 | 0.5005 | 0.683 | 0.528 | 0.220 | 0.311 | 0.880 | 0.696 | 0.009 | 0.988 | 0.063 | 0.628 |\n| 1095\
    \ | 1 | Standardization with Variance Overscaling (1.1x) | Axiom I | 712 | 0.6174 | 0.587 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.780 |\n| 1092 | 1 | MNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing | Axiom I | 710 | 0.5769 | 0.687 | 0.561 | 0.236 | 0.375 | 0.874 | 0.724 | 0.234 | 0.991 | 0.173 | 0.915 |\n| 1091 | 1 | Hybrid v4: Latent Standardization + MNN Residual Correction | Axiom I | 709 | 0.4697 | 0.411 | 0.538 | 0.216 | 0.368 | 0.830 | 0.629 | 0.000 | 0.990 | 0.000 | 0.716 |\n| 1089 | 1 | MNN-based Correction in Latent Space | Axiom I | 707 | 0.5728 | 0.757 | 0.450 | 0.224 | 0.366 | 0.860 | 0.702 | 0.277 | 0.993 | 0.277 | 0.823 |\n| 1087 | 1 | Hybrid v3: Latent Standardization + BBKNN Graph | Axiom I | 706 | 0.1759 | 0.117 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.210 | 0.431 | 0.000 | 1.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1085 | 1 | Latent Space Standardization (Mean and Variance Correction) | Axiom I | 705 | 0.6173 | 0.589 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.991\
    \ | 0.023 | 0.776 |\n| 1082 | 1 | Iterative Centroid Alignment in PCA Space | Axiom I | 703 | 0.5787 | 0.462 | 0.624 | 0.221 | 0.348 | 0.888 | 0.671 | 0.979 | 0.991 | 0.006 | 0.599 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
