tick: 734
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Research Counter. I will now implement and submit my new experimental variant of the Ensemble Correction method.\n\nThis version will replace the MNN-based smoothing component (`E_local`) with a new one based on BBKNN graph smoothing. The core idea is to generate the locally-correct embedding by averaging the PCA coordinates of cells and their neighbors as defined by a BBKNN graph. This `E_local_graph` will then be fused with the globally-correct `E_global` from Latent Space Standardization, using the optimal `alpha=0.6` that I have previously identified.\n\nThis experiment tests a fundamental component of my SOTA framework and could lead to a more elegant and potentially higher-performing model.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ensemble v2: Standardization + BBKNN Graph Smoothing\"\ntags: \"ensemble, standardization, bbknn, graph-smoothing, sotw-refinement\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests a new variant of the SOTA 'Ensemble Correction' framework.\
    \ It replaces the MNN-based local correction component with one based on BBKNN graph smoothing. A locally-aware embedding is generated by averaging the PCA coordinates of cells over their neighborhood in a BBKNN graph. This is then fused with the standard globally-correct embedding using the optimal alpha of 0.6. The goal is to see if this alternative local correction can improve upon the current SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  \"\"\"\n  Ensemble Correction v2: Fusing a Globally-Correct Embedding with a\n  BBKNN Graph-Smoothed Local Embedding.\n\n  This method tests a new way to generate the local correction embedding (E_local).\n  1. E_global: Latent Space Standardization is used as before.\n  2. E_local: A BBKNN graph is built on the original PCA. The E_local embedding\n     is then generated by smoothing the PCA coordinates over this graph.\n  3. The final embedding is a weighted average using the optimal alpha=0.6.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy\
    \ as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  def _build_bbknn_connectivities(X_pca, batch_labels, neighbors_within_batch=3):\n      \"\"\"Helper function to build a BBKNN connectivity matrix.\"\"\"\n      n_cells = X_pca.shape[0]\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n      \n      connectivities = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n      \n      for batch in unique_batches:\n          batch_indices = np.where(batch_labels == batch)[0]\n          if len(batch_indices) == 0: continue\n          \n          batch_pca = X_pca[batch_indices]\n          k = min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, len(batch_indices))\n          nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, n_jobs=1).fit(batch_pca)\n          _, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca)\n          \n          for i in range(n_cells):\n              global_neighbor_indices = batch_indices[indices_all[i]]\n              connectivities[i,\
    \ global_neighbor_indices] = 1\n              \n      return connectivities.tocsr().maximum(connectivities.T)\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Ensemble v2 (BBKNN Graph Smoothing): Starting...\")\n\n      # --- Parameters ---\n      alpha = 0.6\n      n_pcs = 50\n      neighbors_within_batch = 3\n\n      # === STAGE 1: Initial PCA ===\n      print(\"  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization and PCA...\")\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n      n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n      sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n      X_pca_original = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n\n      # === STAGE 2A: Compute E_global (Latent Space Standardization) ===\n      print(\"  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Standardization)...\")\n      E_global = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n\
    \      for pc_idx in range(X_pca_original.shape[1]):\n          pc = X_pca_original[:, pc_idx]\n          g_mean, g_std = pc.mean(), pc.std()\n          for batch in unique_batches:\n              mask = batch_labels == batch\n              if np.any(mask):\n                  b_pc = pc[mask]\n                  b_mean, b_std = b_pc.mean(), b_pc.std()\n                  if b_std < 1e-8: b_std = 1.0\n                  std_pc = (b_pc - b_mean) / b_std\n                  E_global[mask, pc_idx] = std_pc * g_std + g_mean\n      \n      # === STAGE 2B: Compute E_local (BBKNN Graph Smoothing) ===\n      print(\"  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (BBKNN Graph Smoothing)...\")\n      # Build BBKNN graph on the original PCA space\n      bbknn_conn = _build_bbknn_connectivities(X_pca_original, batch_labels, neighbors_within_batch)\n      \n      # Normalize connectivities for averaging (A_hat = D^-1 * A)\n      D_inv = np.array(1.0 / bbknn_conn.sum(axis=1)).flatten()\n      D_inv[np.isinf(D_inv)]\
    \ = 0\n      norm_bbknn_conn = bbknn_conn.multiply(D_inv[:, np.newaxis])\n      \n      # Smooth the PCA coordinates using the graph\n      # This is a single step of label propagation / graph convolution\n      E_local_graph = norm_bbknn_conn @ X_pca_original\n      \n      # === STAGE 3: Fuse Embeddings ===\n      print(f\"  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha={alpha}...\")\n      E_final = (alpha * E_global) + ((1 - alpha) * E_local_graph)\n\n      # === STAGE 4: Create Output ===\n      output = ad.AnnData(\n          obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n          obsm={'X_emb': E_final.astype(np.float32)},\n          uns={'method_id': 'ensemble_std_bbknn_smooth'}\n      )\n      \n      print(f\"✓ Ensemble v2 complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
