tick: 736
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 736\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 140,324 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 46 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Ensemble v2: Standardization + BBKNN Graph Smoothing' (ID: 1112) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6261866379781011\n**ASW_batch:** 0.609\n**ASW_label:** 0.248\n**ARI:** 0.620\n**NMI:** 0.706\n**Graph_conn:** 0.896\n**kBET:** 0.837\n**iLISI:** 0.071\n**cLISI:** 0.992\n**PCR:** 0.914\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.369\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.609  ASW_label: 0.248  ARI: 0.620  NMI: 0.706\n  Graph_conn: 0.896  kBET: 0.837  iLISI: 0.071  cLISI: 0.992\n  PCR: 0.914  Cell_cycle: 0.369\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n\
    \  ASW_batch: 0.807674  ASW_label: 0.554751  ARI: 0.619956  NMI: 0.706554\n  Graph_conn: 0.897868  kBET: 0.798132  iLISI: 0.070699  cLISI: 0.997632\n  PCR: 0.914471  Cell_cycle: 0.323202\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1112\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed missing import error. The code now runs successfully and achieved a score of 0.6262.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission used `lil_matrix` from scipy.sparse to build a sparse connectivity matrix for the BBKNN graph, but failed to import it. The code only imported `issparse` from scipy.sparse:\n```python\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\n```\n\nThis caused a `NameError: name 'lil_matrix' is not defined` at line 24 in `_build_bbknn_connectivities()`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded `lil_matrix` to the scipy.sparse import statement in `submissions/submission_v2.py`:\n```python\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse, lil_matrix\n```\n\nThis was a simple one-line fix that resolved the import error without requiring\
    \ any changes to the algorithm logic.\n\n## Result\n- **Status**: Code executes successfully without crashes\n- **Score**: 0.6261866379781011\n- **Fix Version**: submission_v2.py\n- **Evaluation**: The ensemble method combining global standardization with BBKNN graph smoothing now runs to completion\n\nThe agent's algorithm is sound - it just had a missing import that prevented execution.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nEnsemble Correction v2: Fusing a Globally-Correct Embedding with a\nBBKNN Graph-Smoothed Local Embedding.\n\nThis method tests a new way to generate the local correction embedding (E_local).\n1. E_global: Latent Space Standardization is used as before.\n2. E_local: A BBKNN graph is built on the original PCA. The E_local embedding\n   is then generated by smoothing the\
    \ PCA coordinates over this graph.\n3. The final embedding is a weighted average using the optimal alpha=0.6.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse, lil_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef _build_bbknn_connectivities(X_pca, batch_labels, neighbors_within_batch=3):\n    \"\"\"Helper function to build a BBKNN connectivity matrix.\"\"\"\n    n_cells = X_pca.shape[0]\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n\n    connectivities = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for batch in unique_batches:\n        batch_indices = np.where(batch_labels == batch)[0]\n        if len(batch_indices) == 0: continue\n\n        batch_pca = X_pca[batch_indices]\n        k = min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, len(batch_indices))\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, n_jobs=1).fit(batch_pca)\n        _, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(X_pca)\n\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n\
    \            global_neighbor_indices = batch_indices[indices_all[i]]\n            connectivities[i, global_neighbor_indices] = 1\n\n    return connectivities.tocsr().maximum(connectivities.T)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Ensemble v2 (BBKNN Graph Smoothing): Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Parameters ---\n    alpha = 0.6\n    n_pcs = 50\n    neighbors_within_batch = 3\n\n    # === STAGE 1: Initial PCA ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization and PCA...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca_original = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n\n    # === STAGE 2A: Compute E_global (Latent Space Standardization) ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Standardization)...\"\
    )\n    E_global = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n    for pc_idx in range(X_pca_original.shape[1]):\n        pc = X_pca_original[:, pc_idx]\n        g_mean, g_std = pc.mean(), pc.std()\n        for batch in unique_batches:\n            mask = batch_labels == batch\n            if np.any(mask):\n                b_pc = pc[mask]\n                b_mean, b_std = b_pc.mean(), b_pc.std()\n                if b_std < 1e-8: b_std = 1.0\n                std_pc = (b_pc - b_mean) / b_std\n                E_global[mask, pc_idx] = std_pc * g_std + g_mean\n\n    # === STAGE 2B: Compute E_local (BBKNN Graph Smoothing) ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (BBKNN Graph Smoothing)...\")\n    # Build BBKNN graph on the original PCA space\n    bbknn_conn = _build_bbknn_connectivities(X_pca_original, batch_labels, neighbors_within_batch)\n\n    # Normalize connectivities for averaging (A_hat = D^-1 * A)\n    D_inv = np.array(1.0 / bbknn_conn.sum(axis=1)).flatten()\n    D_inv[np.isinf(D_inv)]\
    \ = 0\n    norm_bbknn_conn = bbknn_conn.multiply(D_inv[:, np.newaxis])\n\n    # Smooth the PCA coordinates using the graph\n    # This is a single step of label propagation / graph convolution\n    E_local_graph = norm_bbknn_conn @ X_pca_original\n\n    # === STAGE 3: Fuse Embeddings ===\n    print(f\"  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha={alpha}...\")\n    E_final = (alpha * E_global) + ((1 - alpha) * E_local_graph)\n\n    # === STAGE 4: Create Output ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': E_final.astype(np.float32)},\n        uns={'method_id': 'ensemble_std_bbknn_smooth'}\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Ensemble v2 complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration\
    \ ===\nEnsemble v2 (BBKNN Graph Smoothing): Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization and PCA...\n  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Standardization)...\n  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (BBKNN Graph Smoothing)...\n  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha=0.6...\n✓ Ensemble v2 complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c2f9715d-9141-4c61-9988-d81c02a39fde/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c2f9715d-9141-4c61-9988-d81c02a39fde\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nWhen the context length becomes long, some agents may begin to forget the Codex. If you notice yourself—or other agents—using phrases like `fundamental barrier` or `impossible`, take it as a serious red flag. Correct yourself, or help others correct themselves.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n###\
    \ Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1112 | 1 | Ensemble v2: Standardization + BBKNN Graph Smoothing | Axiom I | 734 | 0.6262 | 0.620 | 0.609 | 0.248 | 0.369 | 0.896 | 0.706 | 0.914 | 0.992 | 0.071 | 0.837 |\n| 1109 | 1 | Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.5) | Axiom I | 728 | 0.6340 | 0.693 | 0.647 | 0.237 | 0.371 | 0.883 | 0.737 | 0.815 | 0.992 | 0.161 | 0.804 |\n| 1108 | 1 | Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.6) | Axiom I | 726 | 0.6344\
    \ | 0.678 | 0.655 | 0.235 | 0.371 | 0.886 | 0.729 | 0.884 | 0.992 | 0.120 | 0.794 |\n| 1107 | 1 | Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.7) | Axiom I | 724 | 0.6291 | 0.648 | 0.656 | 0.232 | 0.370 | 0.881 | 0.713 | 0.936 | 0.993 | 0.086 | 0.777 |\n| 1106 | 1 | Ensemble Correction (Standardization and MNN Fusion) | Axiom I | 723 | 0.6270 | 0.627 | 0.654 | 0.228 | 0.370 | 0.885 | 0.710 | 0.973 | 0.992 | 0.062 | 0.770 |\n| 1102 | 1 | Graph Correction with a Penalized Distance Metric | Axiom I | 718 | 0.2940 | 0.415 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.899 | 0.635 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.000 | 0.000 |\n| 1100 | 1 | Standardization with Targeted Variance Overscaling | Axiom I | 716 | 0.6174 | 0.579 | 0.627 | 0.210 | 0.409 | 0.877 | 0.681 | 1.000 | 0.990 | 0.021 | 0.780 |\n| 1098 | 1 | Canonical Correlation Analysis (CCA) based Correction | Axiom I | 714 | 0.5005 | 0.683 | 0.528 | 0.220 | 0.311 | 0.880 | 0.696 | 0.009 | 0.988 | 0.063 | 0.628 |\n| 1095 | 1 | Standardization with Variance Overscaling (1.1x) | Axiom\
    \ I | 712 | 0.6174 | 0.587 | 0.648 | 0.220 | 0.368 | 0.873 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.991 | 0.023 | 0.780 |\n| 1092 | 1 | MNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing | Axiom I | 710 | 0.5769 | 0.687 | 0.561 | 0.236 | 0.375 | 0.874 | 0.724 | 0.234 | 0.991 | 0.173 | 0.915 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line\
    \ when executing actions."
