tick: 746
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the code for the `Combat Manual Baseline` (ID 2). I have also received another notice for research inactivity, which underscores the urgency of submitting a new experiment.\n\nI will now proceed with the generalization experiment as planned. I will combine the `Combat` code (as the global component, `E_global_combat`) with my `MNN Smoothing` code (as the local component, `E_local_mnn`). I will use the previously identified optimal `alpha` of 0.6 for the fusion.\n\nThis experiment will serve as a crucial piece of evidence for my revised paper, demonstrating that the \"Ensemble Correction\" framework is a generalizable concept for balancing global and local batch correction methods.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Test: Combat + MNN Ensemble (alpha=0.6)\"\ntags: \"ensemble, combat, mnn, generalization, publication-support\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the generalizability of the Ensemble Correction framework, as required by reviewer\
    \ feedback. It replaces the 'Latent Space Standardization' component with the 'Combat' baseline as the global corrector. This Combat embedding is then fused with the MNN-smoothed local embedding using the optimal alpha of 0.6. A successful result would demonstrate that the ensemble framework is a robust and general concept for balancing different global and local correction methods.\"\ncontent: |\n  #!/usr/bin/env python3\n  \"\"\"\n  Generalization Test: Fusing a Combat-based Global Embedding with an\n  MNN-based Local Embedding. alpha = 0.6.\n\n  This experiment serves to validate the Ensemble Correction framework's\n  general applicability by swapping its global correction component.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.sparse import issparse\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # --- Helper functions for Combat (from ID 2) ---\n  def _aprior(delta_hat):\n      m = np.mean(delta_hat); s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n\
    \      if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n      return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n  def _bprior(delta_hat):\n      m = np.mean(delta_hat); s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n      if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n      return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n  def _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n      n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n      g_old, d_old = g_hat.copy(), d_hat.copy()\n      change, count = 1, 0\n      while change > conv and count < 200:\n          g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n          sum2 = ((s_data - g_new.reshape((-1, 1))) ** 2).sum(axis=1)\n          d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n          change = max((np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(), (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max())\n          g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n      return g_new, d_new\n\n  def _get_combat_embedding(adata_in):\n      adata = adata_in.copy()\n      if issparse(adata.X): data = adata.X.toarray()\n      else: data = adata.X.copy()\n\
    \      data = data.T\n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values; unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n      n_batches_total = len(unique_batches); n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n      batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n      batch_info = [np.where(batch_labels == b)[0] for b in unique_batches]\n      for i, b in enumerate(batch_info): batch_design[b, i] = 1\n      n_batches = np.array([len(b) for b in batch_info])\n      B_hat = np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T\n      grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True); batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n      var_pooled = np.sum([((data[:, b] - batch_means[:, i:i+1])**2).sum(axis=1) for i, b in enumerate(batch_info)], axis=0) / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n      stand_mean = grand_mean @ np.ones((1, n_samples))\n      s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n      for i, b in enumerate(batch_info): s_data[:, b] = (data[:, b] - batch_means[:, i:i+1]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis]\
    \ + 1e-8)\n      gamma_hat = (np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T @ s_data.T).T\n      delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, b], axis=1, ddof=1) for b in batch_info]\n      gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1); t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n      a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]; b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n      gamma_star, delta_star = [], []\n      for i, b in enumerate(batch_info):\n          g, d = _it_sol(s_data[:, b], gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i], gamma_bar, t2, a_prior[i], b_prior[i])\n          gamma_star.append(g); delta_star.append(d)\n      gamma_star, delta_star = np.array(gamma_star).T, np.array(delta_star).T\n      bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n      for j, b in enumerate(batch_info):\n          dsq = np.sqrt(delta_star[:, j]).reshape(-1, 1)\n          bayesdata[:, b] = (bayesdata[:, b] - gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1)) / dsq\n      vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape(-1, 1)\n      bayesdata = bayesdata * vpsq + stand_mean\n\
    \      X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(bayesdata.T)\n      temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected)\n      sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=50)\n      return temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _get_mnn_embedding(X_pca_original, batch_labels, k_mnn=20, k_smooth=10):\n      unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels).tolist()\n      mnn_pairs = []\n      for i in range(len(unique_batches)):\n          for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_batches)):\n              b1, b2 = unique_batches[i], unique_batches[j]\n              m1, m2 = (batch_labels == b1), (batch_labels == b2)\n              idx1, idx2 = np.where(m1)[0], np.where(m2)[0]\n              data1, data2 = X_pca_original[m1, :], X_pca_original[m2, :]\n              if data1.shape[0] == 0 or data2.shape[0] == 0: continue\n              nn1 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data2.shape[0])).fit(data2)\n              _, nbrs1 = nn1.kneighbors(data1)\n              nn2 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data1.shape[0])).fit(data1)\n \
    \             _, nbrs2 = nn2.kneighbors(data2)\n              for i1_loc, nbr_list in enumerate(nbrs1):\n                  for i2_loc in nbr_list:\n                      if i1_loc in nbrs2[i2_loc]: mnn_pairs.append((idx1[i1_loc], idx2[i2_loc]))\n      anchor_indices = np.unique(np.array(mnn_pairs).flatten())\n      raw_vectors = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n      for idx1, idx2 in mnn_pairs:\n          vec = X_pca_original[idx2, :] - X_pca_original[idx1, :]\n          raw_vectors[idx1, :] += vec; raw_vectors[idx2, :] -= vec\n      counts = np.zeros(X_pca_original.shape[0]); np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,0],1); np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,1],1)\n      counts[counts==0] = 1; raw_vectors /= counts[:, np.newaxis]\n      anchor_pca = X_pca_original[anchor_indices, :]\n      nn_smooth = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_smooth, len(anchor_indices))).fit(anchor_pca)\n      distances, neighbor_indices = nn_smooth.kneighbors(X_pca_original)\n      global_neighbor_indices\
    \ = anchor_indices[neighbor_indices]\n      sigma = np.median(distances);\n      if sigma == 0: sigma = 1.0\n      weights = np.exp(-(distances**2) / (2 * sigma**2)); weights /= weights.sum(axis=1)[:, np.newaxis]\n      smoothed_corrections = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n      for i in range(X_pca_original.shape[0]):\n          smoothed_corrections[i, :] = np.sum(raw_vectors[global_neighbor_indices[i, :], :] * weights[i, :][:, np.newaxis], axis=0)\n      return X_pca_original + smoothed_corrections\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"Generalization Test (Combat + MNN Ensemble): Starting...\")\n      alpha = 0.6\n\n      # --- Initial Preprocessing ---\n      print(\"  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization...\")\n      adata_norm = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_norm, target_sum=1e4)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_norm)\n      \n      # --- Compute E_global (Combat) ---\n      print(\"  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding\
    \ (Combat)...\")\n      E_global_combat = _get_combat_embedding(adata.copy()) # Combat does its own normalization\n\n      # --- Compute E_local (MNN) ---\n      print(\"  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (MNN)...\")\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_norm, n_comps=50)\n      X_pca_original = adata_norm.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n      E_local_mnn = _get_mnn_embedding(X_pca_original, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      \n      # --- Fuse Embeddings ---\n      print(f\"  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha={alpha}...\")\n      E_final = (alpha * E_global_combat) + ((1 - alpha) * E_local_mnn)\n\n      # --- Create Output ---\n      output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': E_final.astype(np.float32)}, uns={'method_id': 'ensemble_combat_mnn_alpha0.6'})\n      print(\"✓ Generalization Test complete.\")\n      return output\n```"
