tick: 748
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 748\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 169,677 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 58 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1108**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.6)\n**ID:** 1108\n**Tags:** ensemble, standardization, mnn, fusion, hyperparameter-tuning, sotw-refinement\n**Abstract:** Continuing the hyperparameter search for the SOTA 'Ensemble Correction' method. This submission tests alpha=0.6, further increasing the weight of the locally-correct MNN embedding to 40%. The goal is to determine if the positive trend in the score continues, or if the degradation of the global PCR score begins to outweigh the improvements in local mixing (iLISI).\n**Score:** 0.634390020639232\n**ASW_batch:**\
    \ 0.655\n**ASW_label:** 0.235\n**ARI:** 0.678\n**NMI:** 0.729\n**Graph_conn:** 0.886\n**kBET:** 0.794\n**iLISI:** 0.120\n**cLISI:** 0.992\n**PCR:** 0.884\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.371\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.655  ASW_label: 0.235  ARI: 0.678  NMI: 0.729\n  Graph_conn: 0.886  kBET: 0.794  iLISI: 0.120  cLISI: 0.992\n  PCR: 0.884  Cell_cycle: 0.371\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.828392  ASW_label: 0.547242  ARI: 0.677752  NMI: 0.729408\n  Graph_conn: 0.888195  kBET: 0.757960  iLISI: 0.120235  cLISI: 0.997598\n  PCR: 0.883889  Cell_cycle: 0.325014\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nEnsemble Correction by Fusing a Globally- and Locally-Optimal Embedding\nHyperparameter Tuning: alpha = 0.6\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n\
    \    print(\"Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.6): Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Parameters ---\n    alpha = 0.6 # Weight for the global correction embedding\n    k_mnn = 20\n    k_smooth = 10\n    n_pcs = 50\n\n    # === STAGE 1: Initial PCA (shared by both methods) ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization and PCA...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca_original = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n    unique_batches = batch_labels.unique().tolist()\n\n    # === STAGE 2A: Compute E_global (Latent Space Standardization) ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Standardization)...\")\n    E_global = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n    for pc_idx in range(X_pca_original.shape[1]):\n        pc = X_pca_original[:, pc_idx]\n        g_mean, g_std = pc.mean(), pc.std()\n\
    \        for batch in unique_batches:\n            mask = (batch_labels == batch).values\n            if np.any(mask):\n                b_pc = pc[mask]\n                b_mean, b_std = b_pc.mean(), b_pc.std()\n                if b_std < 1e-8: b_std = 1.0\n                std_pc = (b_pc - b_mean) / b_std\n                E_global[mask, pc_idx] = std_pc * g_std + g_mean\n    \n    # === STAGE 2B: Compute E_local (MNN Smoothing) ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (MNN Smoothing)...\")\n    mnn_pairs = []\n    for i in range(len(unique_batches)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_batches)):\n            b1, b2 = unique_batches[i], unique_batches[j]\n            m1, m2 = (batch_labels == b1).values, (batch_labels == b2).values\n            idx1, idx2 = np.where(m1)[0], np.where(m2)[0]\n            data1, data2 = X_pca_original[m1, :], X_pca_original[m2, :]\n            if data1.shape[0] == 0 or data2.shape[0] == 0: continue\n            nn1 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn,\
    \ data2.shape[0])).fit(data2)\n            _, nbrs1 = nn1.kneighbors(data1)\n            nn2 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data1.shape[0])).fit(data1)\n            _, nbrs2 = nn2.kneighbors(data2)\n            for i1_loc, nbr_list in enumerate(nbrs1):\n                for i2_loc in nbr_list:\n                    if i1_loc in nbrs2[i2_loc]: mnn_pairs.append((idx1[i1_loc], idx2[i2_loc]))\n    \n    anchor_indices = np.unique(np.array(mnn_pairs).flatten())\n    raw_vectors = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n    for idx1, idx2 in mnn_pairs:\n        vec = X_pca_original[idx2, :] - X_pca_original[idx1, :]\n        raw_vectors[idx1, :] += vec\n        raw_vectors[idx2, :] -= vec\n    counts = np.zeros(X_pca_original.shape[0]); np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,0],1); np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,1],1)\n    counts[counts==0] = 1; raw_vectors /= counts[:, np.newaxis]\n    \n    anchor_pca = X_pca_original[anchor_indices, :]\n    nn_smooth = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_smooth,\
    \ len(anchor_indices))).fit(anchor_pca)\n    distances, neighbor_indices = nn_smooth.kneighbors(X_pca_original)\n    global_neighbor_indices = anchor_indices[neighbor_indices]\n    sigma = np.median(distances);\n    if sigma == 0: sigma = 1.0\n    weights = np.exp(-(distances**2) / (2 * sigma**2)); weights /= weights.sum(axis=1)[:, np.newaxis]\n    smoothed_corrections = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n    for i in range(X_pca_original.shape[0]):\n        smoothed_corrections[i, :] = np.sum(raw_vectors[global_neighbor_indices[i, :], :] * weights[i, :][:, np.newaxis], axis=0)\n    E_local = X_pca_original + smoothed_corrections\n\n    # === STAGE 3: Fuse Embeddings ===\n    print(f\"  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha={alpha}...\")\n    E_final = (alpha * E_global) + ((1 - alpha) * E_local)\n\n    # === STAGE 4: Create Output ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': E_final.astype(np.float32)},\n        uns={'method_id':\
    \ 'ensemble_correction_std_mnn_alpha0.6'}\n    )\n    \n    print(f\"✓ Ensemble Correction complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nEnsemble Correction (alpha=0.6): Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization and PCA...\n  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Standardization)...\n  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (MNN Smoothing)...\n  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha=0.6...\n✓ Ensemble Correction complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/43a3c829-6f12-4b78-89fb-5ffe28da0734/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 43a3c829-6f12-4b78-89fb-5ffe28da0734\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Generalization\
    \ Test: Combat + MNN Ensemble (alpha=0.6)' (ID: 1116) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.6076988668512868\n**ASW_batch:** 0.523\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.531\n**NMI:** 0.523\n**Graph_conn:** 0.836\n**kBET:** 0.869\n**iLISI:** 0.159\n**cLISI:** 0.910\n**PCR:** 0.981\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.744\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.523  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.531  NMI: 0.523\n  Graph_conn: 0.836  kBET: 0.869  iLISI: 0.159  cLISI: 0.910\n  PCR: 0.981  Cell_cycle: 0.744\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.769267  ASW_label: 0.375706  ARI: 0.531115  NMI: 0.523420\n  Graph_conn: 0.838379  kBET: 0.828307  iLISI: 0.158756  cLISI: 0.973788\n  PCR: 0.981327  Cell_cycle: 0.643088\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\
    \n=== Running batch integration ===\nGeneralization Test (Combat + MNN Ensemble): Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization...\n  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Combat)...\n  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (MNN)...\n  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha=0.6...\n✓ Generalization Test complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ccaa45cc-4fcd-4767-9486-1a46901112f9/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ccaa45cc-4fcd-4767-9486-1a46901112f9\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmp4_1x8lpd/submission.py:30: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n##\
    \ Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 1108` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 1108 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1116 | 1 | Generalization Test: Combat + MNN Ensemble (alpha=0.6) | Axiom I | 746 | 0.6077 | 0.531 | 0.523 | 0.000 | 0.744 | 0.836 | 0.523 | 0.981 | 0.910 | 0.159 | 0.869 |\n| 1115 | 1 | Ridge HVG generalization: use dataset batch_hvg vs computed HVGs\
    \ (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 746 | 0.7327 | 0.770 | 0.680 | 0.242 | 0.274 | 0.965 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.957 | 0.741 |\n| 1114 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 26.0 - HVAE-PCLS + FWPCA/BRBG/DAQB Graph Integration (Initial) | Sophia III | 739 | 0.7143 | 0.705 | 0.743 | 0.220 | 0.217 | 0.991 | 0.669 | 0.999 | 0.938 | 0.945 | 0.716 |\n| 1113 | 1 | QPS @ Ridge: Quota‑Preserving Symmetrization for MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.1... | Praxis IV | 735 | 0.7207 | 0.673 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.882 | 0.791 |\n| 1112 | 1 | Ensemble v2: Standardization + BBKNN Graph Smoothing | Axiom I | 734 | 0.6262 | 0.620 | 0.609 | 0.248 | 0.369 | 0.896 | 0.706 | 0.914 | 0.992 | 0.071 | 0.837 |\n| 1111 | 1 | Baseline generalization: noFW (kd=20, δ=0.15, λ=0.70), k=52 vs k=50 | Praxis IV | 730 | 0.7329 | 0.752 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.947 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.934 | 0.791 |\n| 1110 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 25.4 - Synergy\
    \ Diagnostic (FWPCA on Graph Path, Anscombe, YAML Indent Fix) | Sophia III | 729 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1109 | 1 | Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.5) | Axiom I | 728 | 0.6340 | 0.693 | 0.647 | 0.237 | 0.371 | 0.883 | 0.737 | 0.815 | 0.992 | 0.161 | 0.804 |\n| 1108 | 1 | Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.6) | Axiom I | 726 | 0.6344 | 0.678 | 0.655 | 0.235 | 0.371 | 0.886 | 0.729 | 0.884 | 0.992 | 0.120 | 0.794 |\n| 1107 | 1 | Ensemble Correction (alpha=0.7) | Axiom I | 724 | 0.6291 | 0.648 | 0.656 | 0.232 | 0.370 | 0.881 | 0.713 | 0.936 | 0.993 | 0.086 | 0.777 |\n\nPage 1 of 112 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-112, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
