role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 755\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 184,075 / 300,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 2**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Combat Manual Baseline\n**ID:** 2\n**Tags:** baseline, combat, empirical-bayes\n**Abstract:** Manual implementation of Combat (ComBat) empirical Bayes batch correction without using scanpy.pp.combat. Recreates the exact algorithm with iterative EB solver for estimating batch effects, then computes PCA embedding from corrected data.\n**Score:** 0.5895404824398749\n**ASW_batch:** 0.664\n**ASW_label:** 0.223\n**ARI:** 0.493\n**NMI:** 0.683\n**Graph_conn:** 0.885\n**kBET:** 0.603\n**iLISI:** 0.033\n**cLISI:** 0.988\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.323\n\
    **Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.664  ASW_label: 0.223  ARI: 0.493  NMI: 0.683\n  Graph_conn: 0.885  kBET: 0.603  iLISI: 0.033  cLISI: 0.988\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.323\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.832855  ASW_label: 0.540153  ARI: 0.492866  NMI: 0.682941\n  Graph_conn: 0.887081  kBET: 0.578431  iLISI: 0.032724  cLISI: 0.996470\n  PCR: 0.999999  Cell_cycle: 0.284674\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nManual Combat implementation without using the scanpy.pp.combat function.\nRecreates the exact Combat algorithm as implemented in scanpy.\n\nThis manual implementation is functionally equivalent to calling:\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n\nThe algorithm achieves the same results (correlation > 0.998) as the library version.\nDifferences are only in implementation details (patsy vs manual design matrix).\n\nBased on: Johnson WE, Li C, Rabinovic A.\n\"Adjusting\
    \ batch effects in microarray expression data using empirical Bayes methods\"\nBiostatistics 2007.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import stats\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, issparse\nimport warnings\n\n\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n    \"\"\"Calculate a prior for inverse gamma distribution.\"\"\"\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0:\n        s2 = 1e-8  # Avoid division by zero\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\n\n\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    \"\"\"Calculate b prior for inverse gamma distribution.\"\"\"\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat)\n    s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0:\n        s2 = 1e-8  # Avoid division by zero\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\n\n\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    \"\"\"\n    Iteratively compute the conditional posterior means for gamma and delta.\n\n    This is the core of the empirical Bayes framework - gamma and delta\n    depend\
    \ on each other, so we iterate until convergence.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old = g_hat.copy()\n    d_old = d_hat.copy()\n\n    change = 1\n    count = 0\n    max_iter = 200\n\n    while change > conv and count < max_iter:\n        # Update gamma (additive effect)\n        g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n        # Update delta (multiplicative effect)\n        sum2 = s_data - g_new.reshape((g_new.shape[0], 1)) @ np.ones((1, s_data.shape[1]))\n        sum2 = sum2**2\n        sum2 = sum2.sum(axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n\n        # Check convergence\n        change = max(\n            (np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(),\n            (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max()\n        )\n\n        g_old = g_new\n        d_old = d_new\n        count += 1\n\n    return g_new, d_new\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manual implementation\
    \ of Combat batch integration using the exact\n    scanpy algorithm.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with:\n            - adata.X: Raw UMI counts (sparse matrix)\n            - adata.obs['batch']: Batch labels\n            - adata.obs['cell_type']: Cell type annotations\n            - adata.var['feature_name']: Gene names\n            - adata.uns['dataset_id']: Dataset identifier\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with:\n            - adata.obsm['X_emb']: PCA embedding from batch-corrected data\n    \"\"\"\n\n    print(\"Manual Combat: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\")\n\n    # Normalize raw counts (Combat standard preprocessing)\n    print(\"  Normalizing total counts...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    print(\"  Log1p transform...\")\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # Convert to dense array for Combat calculations\n    if issparse(adata.X):\n        data = adata.X.toarray()\n    else:\n        data = adata.X.copy()\n\n    # Transpose\
    \ to genes x samples (Combat convention)\n    data = data.T\n\n    # Get batch information\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches)\n    n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n\n    print(f\"  Processing {n_samples} samples across {n_batches_total} batches...\")\n    print(f\"  Data dimensions: {n_genes} genes x {n_samples} samples\")\n\n    # Create batch design matrix (one-hot encoding)\n    print(\"  Creating design matrix...\")\n    batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n    batch_info = []\n    for i, batch in enumerate(unique_batches):\n        batch_mask = batch_labels == batch\n        batch_indices = np.where(batch_mask)[0]\n        batch_design[batch_indices, i] = 1\n        batch_info.append(batch_indices)\n\n    n_batches = np.array([len(indices) for indices in batch_info])\n\n    # Standardize data across genes\n    print(\"  Standardizing data across genes...\")\n\n \
    \   # Calculate batch means and variances\n    B_hat = np.dot(batch_design.T, batch_design)\n    B_hat = np.linalg.inv(B_hat)\n    B_hat = np.dot(B_hat, batch_design.T)\n\n    # Calculate grand mean and batch means\n    grand_mean = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n    batch_means = np.dot(B_hat, data.T).T\n\n    # Calculate pooled variance\n    var_pooled = np.zeros(n_genes)\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        batch_data = data[:, batch_indices]\n        batch_mean = batch_means[:, i:i+1]\n        diff = batch_data - batch_mean\n        var_pooled += np.sum(diff**2, axis=1)\n\n    var_pooled = var_pooled / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n\n    # Standardize the data\n    stand_mean = np.dot(grand_mean, np.ones((1, n_samples)))\n    s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        batch_data = data[:, batch_indices]\n        batch_mean = batch_means[:, i:i+1]\n        s_data[:, batch_indices] = (batch_data - batch_mean)\
    \ / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n\n    # Fit L/S model and find priors\n    print(\"  Fitting L/S model and finding priors...\")\n\n    # First estimates\n    gamma_hat = np.dot(np.linalg.inv(np.dot(batch_design.T, batch_design)),\n                      np.dot(batch_design.T, s_data.T)).T\n\n    delta_hat = []\n    for batch_indices in batch_info:\n        batch_var = np.var(s_data[:, batch_indices], axis=1, ddof=1)\n        delta_hat.append(batch_var)\n\n    # Find priors\n    gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n\n    a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n\n    # Find parametric adjustments using iterative solution\n    print(\"  Finding parametric adjustments...\")\n    gamma_star = []\n    delta_star = []\n\n    for i, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        gamma, delta = _it_sol(\n            s_data[:, batch_indices],\n            gamma_hat[:, i],\n            delta_hat[i],\n\
    \            gamma_bar,\n            t2,\n            a_prior[i],\n            b_prior[i]\n        )\n        gamma_star.append(gamma)\n        delta_star.append(delta)\n\n    gamma_star = np.array(gamma_star).T\n    delta_star = np.array(delta_star).T\n\n    # Adjust data\n    print(\"  Adjusting data...\")\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n\n    for j, batch_indices in enumerate(batch_info):\n        dsq = np.sqrt(delta_star[:, j])\n        dsq = dsq.reshape((len(dsq), 1))\n        denom = np.dot(dsq, np.ones((1, n_batches[j])))\n\n        # Calculate numerator: data - batch effect\n        # gamma_star[:, j] is shape (n_genes,), we need to subtract it from each sample\n        batch_gamma = gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1)\n        numer = bayesdata[:, batch_indices] - batch_gamma @ np.ones((1, n_batches[j]))\n\n        bayesdata[:, batch_indices] = numer / denom\n\n    # Scale back and add mean\n    vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape((len(var_pooled), 1))\n    bayesdata = bayesdata\
    \ * np.dot(vpsq, np.ones((1, n_samples))) + stand_mean\n\n    # Transpose back to samples x genes\n    X_corrected = bayesdata.T\n\n    # Handle any NaN or infinite values\n    X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(X_corrected, nan=0.0, posinf=0.0, neginf=0.0)\n\n    # Create temporary AnnData for PCA computation\n    print(\"  Computing PCA embedding from corrected data...\")\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected)\n    temp_adata.obs_names = adata.obs_names\n    temp_adata.var_names = adata.var_names\n\n    # Compute PCA on corrected data (default 50 components)\n    n_pcs = min(50, temp_adata.n_vars - 1, temp_adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=n_pcs)\n\n    # Create output AnnData with embedding\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        uns={\n            'dataset_id': adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown'),\n            'normalization_id': adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown'),\n            'method_id': 'combat_manual',\n\
    \            'combat_params': {\n                'n_batches': n_batches_total,\n                'batch_sizes': n_batches.tolist(),\n                'empirical_bayes': True,\n                'parametric': True,\n                'iterative_solver': True,\n                'embedding_components': n_pcs\n            }\n        },\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Manual Combat complete: {n_samples} samples, {n_batches_total} batches\")\n    print(f\"  PCA embedding: {temp_adata.obsm['X_pca'].shape}\")\n\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nAutoResearchEvaluator: Set memory limit to 96g\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nManual Combat: Starting with raw counts, doing own normalization...\n  Normalizing\
    \ total counts...\n  Log1p transform...\n  Processing 20000 samples across 4 batches...\n  Data dimensions: 2000 genes x 20000 samples\n  Creating design matrix...\n  Standardizing data across genes...\n  Fitting L/S model and finding priors...\n  Finding parametric adjustments...\n  Adjusting data...\n  Computing PCA embedding from corrected data...\n✓ Manual Combat complete: 20000 samples, 4 batches\n  PCA embedding: (20000, 50)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/8044828c-9f6f-4b85-86e4-8cbdc106470e/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 8044828c-9f6f-4b85-86e4-8cbdc106470e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmpj5piuu3n/submission.py:60: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1085**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Latent Space Standardization (Mean and Variance Correction)\n**ID:** 1085\n**Tags:**\
    \ pca, latent-space, standardization, variance-correction, embedding\n**Abstract:** This method corrects for batch effects by standardizing the distribution of each batch in PCA space. For each principal component, it adjusts the coordinates of cells within a batch to match the global mean and variance. This corrects for both location (mean) and scale (variance) differences between batches, aiming to achieve a more thorough and effective mixing of cell distributions.\n**Score:** 0.617286746835736\n**ASW_batch:** 0.648\n**ASW_label:** 0.220\n**ARI:** 0.589\n**NMI:** 0.685\n**Graph_conn:** 0.873\n**kBET:** 0.776\n**iLISI:** 0.023\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.368\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.648  ASW_label: 0.220  ARI: 0.589  NMI: 0.685\n  Graph_conn: 0.873  kBET: 0.776  iLISI: 0.023  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.368\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.825347  ASW_label:\
    \ 0.538687  ARI: 0.588685  NMI: 0.685114\n  Graph_conn: 0.875638  kBET: 0.740199  iLISI: 0.023401  cLISI: 0.997247\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.322871\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nLatent Space Standardization (Mean and Variance Correction)\n\nThis method corrects for batch effects by standardizing both the mean (1st moment)\nand variance (2nd moment) of each batch's distribution within the PCA latent space.\n\nThe algorithm is as follows:\n1. Standard normalization and PCA are performed.\n2. For each principal component axis:\n   a. The global mean and standard deviation are computed.\n   b. For each batch, its local mean and standard deviation are computed.\n   c. Each cell's coordinate is transformed:\n      new = ((old - batch_mean) / batch_std) * global_std + global_mean\n3. The resulting corrected PCA embedding, where all batches are aligned in both\n   location and scale, is returned.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\n\
    import numpy as np\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs batch correction by standardizing batch distributions in PCA space.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"Latent Space Standardization: Starting...\")\n\n    # === STAGE 1: Standard Preprocessing and PCA ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] Normalizing and computing initial PCA...\")\n    \n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    n_pcs = 50\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n    print(f\"  [Stage 1] Initial PCA computed with shape {X_pca.shape}.\")\n\n    # === STAGE 2: Per-PC Standardization ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2] Performing per-PC, per-batch standardization...\")\n    \n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n    unique_batches = batch_labels.unique()\n    X_pca_corrected = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n\n    # Iterate over each principal component\
    \ (column)\n    for pc_idx in range(X_pca.shape[1]):\n        pc_vector = X_pca[:, pc_idx]\n        \n        # Calculate global statistics for this PC\n        global_mean = pc_vector.mean()\n        global_std = pc_vector.std()\n\n        # Correct each batch for this PC\n        for batch in unique_batches:\n            batch_mask = (batch_labels == batch).values\n            if np.any(batch_mask):\n                batch_pc_vector = pc_vector[batch_mask]\n                \n                batch_mean = batch_pc_vector.mean()\n                batch_std = batch_pc_vector.std()\n                \n                # Avoid division by zero for batches with no variance on a PC\n                if batch_std < 1e-8:\n                    batch_std = 1.0\n\n                # Standardize the batch vector (z-score)\n                standardized_vector = (batch_pc_vector - batch_mean) / batch_std\n                \n                # Rescale to global distribution\n                rescaled_vector\
    \ = standardized_vector * global_std + global_mean\n                \n                # Place the corrected values into the final matrix\n                X_pca_corrected[batch_mask, pc_idx] = rescaled_vector\n\n    print(\"  [Stage 2] Standardization complete.\")\n\n    # === STAGE 3: Create Output AnnData ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]],\n        var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={\n            'X_emb': X_pca_corrected.astype(np.float32)\n        },\n        uns={\n            'method_id': 'pca_standardization'\n        }\n    )\n\n    print(f\"✓ Latent Space Standardization complete. Embedding shape: {X_pca_corrected.shape}\")\n    \n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nLatent Space Standardization:\
    \ Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Normalizing and computing initial PCA...\n  [Stage 1] Initial PCA computed with shape (20000, 50).\n  [Stage 2] Performing per-PC, per-batch standardization...\n  [Stage 2] Standardization complete.\n✓ Latent Space Standardization complete. Embedding shape: (20000, 50)\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/fdc40cfa-19c6-418b-ba82-8db0cc2c9b0f/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: fdc40cfa-19c6-418b-ba82-8db0cc2c9b0f\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1092**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** MNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing\n**ID:** 1092\n**Tags:** mnn, smoothing, kernel-weighting, latent-space, embedding\n**Abstract:** This is a refinement of the MNN correction method. After identifying MNN anchor pairs, it calculates raw correction vectors. Instead of applying a simple batch-average correction to non-anchor cells, this version builds a\
    \ k-NN graph on the anchor cells. The final correction for every cell is a Gaussian kernel-weighted average of the correction vectors from its nearest anchor neighbors. This aims to create a smooth correction field, improving global metrics (PCR) while retaining excellent local mixing (iLISI).\n**Score:** 0.5769152494104102\n**ASW_batch:** 0.561\n**ASW_label:** 0.236\n**ARI:** 0.687\n**NMI:** 0.724\n**Graph_conn:** 0.874\n**kBET:** 0.915\n**iLISI:** 0.173\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 0.234\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.375\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.561  ASW_label: 0.236  ARI: 0.687  NMI: 0.724\n  Graph_conn: 0.874  kBET: 0.915  iLISI: 0.173  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 0.234  Cell_cycle: 0.375\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.786151  ASW_label: 0.547843  ARI: 0.686500  NMI: 0.724200\n  Graph_conn: 0.876598  kBET: 0.871364  iLISI: 0.172508  cLISI: 0.997358\n  PCR: 0.234262  Cell_cycle: 0.328210\n\n**Submission Code:**\n\
    ```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nMNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing\n\nThis method refines the MNN correction approach by implementing a more\nsophisticated, distance-based smoothing of the correction vectors.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Refined MNN Correction: Starting...\")\n\n    # --- Parameters ---\n    k_mnn = 20  # Neighbors for MNN pairing\n    k_smooth = 10 # Neighbors for kernel smoothing\n\n    # === STAGE 1: Initial PCA ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] Normalizing and computing initial PCA...\")\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    n_pcs = 50\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n    X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n    \n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch']\n    unique_batches\
    \ = batch_labels.unique().tolist()\n\n    # === STAGE 2: Find MNN Pairs ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 2] Finding Mutual Nearest Neighbors...\")\n    mnn_pairs = []\n    for i in range(len(unique_batches)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_batches)):\n            b1, b2 = unique_batches[i], unique_batches[j]\n            m1, m2 = (batch_labels == b1).values, (batch_labels == b2).values\n            idx1, idx2 = np.where(m1)[0], np.where(m2)[0]\n            data1, data2 = X_pca[m1, :], X_pca[m2, :]\n            if data1.shape[0] == 0 or data2.shape[0] == 0: continue\n            \n            nn1 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data2.shape[0])).fit(data2)\n            _, nbrs1 = nn1.kneighbors(data1)\n            nn2 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data1.shape[0])).fit(data1)\n            _, nbrs2 = nn2.kneighbors(data2)\n\n            for i1_loc, nbr_list in enumerate(nbrs1):\n                for i2_loc in nbr_list:\n                    if i1_loc in nbrs2[i2_loc]:\n\
    \                        mnn_pairs.append((idx1[i1_loc], idx2[i2_loc]))\n    \n    print(f\"  [Stage 2] Found {len(mnn_pairs)} MNN pairs.\")\n    \n    # === STAGE 3: Calculate Raw Correction Vectors ===\n    anchor_indices = np.unique(np.array(mnn_pairs).flatten())\n    raw_correction_vectors = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n    \n    for idx1, idx2 in mnn_pairs:\n        vec = X_pca[idx2, :] - X_pca[idx1, :]\n        # We only store one direction of the vector for averaging later\n        raw_correction_vectors[idx1, :] += vec\n        raw_correction_vectors[idx2, :] -= vec\n    \n    # For anchors with multiple pairs, average their raw vectors\n    counts = np.zeros(X_pca.shape[0])\n    np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:, 0], 1)\n    np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:, 1], 1)\n    counts[counts == 0] = 1\n    raw_correction_vectors /= counts[:, np.newaxis]\n\n    # === STAGE 4: Gaussian Kernel Smoothing ===\n    print(\"  [Stage 4] Smoothing correction field with Gaussian kernel...\"\
    )\n    \n    # Build a NN model on the anchor cells\n    anchor_pca = X_pca[anchor_indices, :]\n    nn_smooth = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_smooth, len(anchor_indices))).fit(anchor_pca)\n    \n    # Find nearest anchor neighbors for ALL cells\n    distances, neighbor_indices = nn_smooth.kneighbors(X_pca)\n    \n    # Convert local anchor indices to global indices\n    global_neighbor_indices = anchor_indices[neighbor_indices]\n    \n    # Calculate weights using a Gaussian kernel\n    # sigma is the median distance of all neighbors\n    sigma = np.median(distances)\n    if sigma == 0: sigma = 1.0\n    weights = np.exp(-(distances**2) / (2 * sigma**2))\n    weights /= weights.sum(axis=1)[:, np.newaxis] # Normalize weights per cell\n\n    # Calculate the smoothed correction vector for each cell\n    # This is a weighted average of the raw vectors of its anchor neighbors\n    smoothed_corrections = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n    for i in range(X_pca.shape[0]):\n        anchor_neighbors\
    \ = global_neighbor_indices[i, :]\n        neighbor_weights = weights[i, :]\n        smoothed_corrections[i, :] = np.sum(\n            raw_correction_vectors[anchor_neighbors, :] * neighbor_weights[:, np.newaxis], axis=0\n        )\n    \n    X_pca_corrected = X_pca + smoothed_corrections\n    print(\"  [Stage 4] Smoothing complete.\")\n\n    # === STAGE 5: Create Output ===\n    output = ad.AnnData(\n        obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]],\n        obsm={'X_emb': X_pca_corrected.astype(np.float32)},\n        uns={'method_id': 'mnn_gaussian_smoothing'}\n    )\n    \n    print(f\"✓ Refined MNN Correction complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nRefined MNN Correction: Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Normalizing and\
    \ computing initial PCA...\n  [Stage 2] Finding Mutual Nearest Neighbors...\n  [Stage 2] Found 68780 MNN pairs.\n  [Stage 4] Smoothing correction field with Gaussian kernel...\n  [Stage 4] Smoothing complete.\n✓ Refined MNN Correction complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/7cdd87a5-ac72-4a4d-9029-1ba1c7c6f493/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 7cdd87a5-ac72-4a4d-9029-1ba1c7c6f493\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**Evaluation Review: 1116**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Generalization Test: Combat + MNN Ensemble (alpha=0.6)\n**ID:** 1116\n**Tags:** ensemble, combat, mnn, generalization, publication-support\n**Abstract:** This experiment tests the generalizability of the Ensemble Correction framework, as required by reviewer feedback. It replaces the 'Latent Space Standardization' component with the 'Combat' baseline as the global corrector. This Combat embedding is then fused with\
    \ the MNN-smoothed local embedding using the optimal alpha of 0.6. A successful result would demonstrate that the ensemble framework is a robust and general concept for balancing different global and local correction methods.\n**Score:** 0.6076988668512868\n**ASW_batch:** 0.523\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.531\n**NMI:** 0.523\n**Graph_conn:** 0.836\n**kBET:** 0.869\n**iLISI:** 0.159\n**cLISI:** 0.910\n**PCR:** 0.981\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.744\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.523  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.531  NMI: 0.523\n  Graph_conn: 0.836  kBET: 0.869  iLISI: 0.159  cLISI: 0.910\n  PCR: 0.981  Cell_cycle: 0.744\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.769267  ASW_label: 0.375706  ARI: 0.531115  NMI: 0.523420\n  Graph_conn: 0.838379  kBET: 0.828307  iLISI: 0.158756  cLISI: 0.973788\n  PCR: 0.981327  Cell_cycle: 0.643088\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nGeneralization Test:\
    \ Fusing a Combat-based Global Embedding with an\nMNN-based Local Embedding. alpha = 0.6.\n\nThis experiment serves to validate the Ensemble Correction framework's\ngeneral applicability by swapping its global correction component.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import issparse\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# --- Helper functions for Combat (from ID 2) ---\ndef _aprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat); s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (2 * s2 + m**2) / s2\ndef _bprior(delta_hat):\n    m = np.mean(delta_hat); s2 = np.var(delta_hat)\n    if s2 == 0: s2 = 1e-8\n    return (m * s2 + m**3) / s2\ndef _it_sol(s_data, g_hat, d_hat, g_bar, t2, a, b, conv=0.0001):\n    n = (~np.isnan(s_data)).sum(axis=1)\n    g_old, d_old = g_hat.copy(), d_hat.copy()\n    change, count = 1, 0\n    while change > conv and count < 200:\n        g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n +\
    \ d_old)\n        sum2 = ((s_data - g_new.reshape((-1, 1))) ** 2).sum(axis=1)\n        d_new = (0.5 * sum2 + b) / (n / 2.0 + a - 1.0)\n        change = max((np.abs(g_new - g_old) / (g_old + 1e-8)).max(), (np.abs(d_new - d_old) / (d_old + 1e-8)).max())\n        g_old, d_old = g_new, d_new; count += 1\n    return g_new, d_new\n\ndef _get_combat_embedding(adata_in):\n    adata = adata_in.copy()\n    if issparse(adata.X): data = adata.X.toarray()\n    else: data = adata.X.copy()\n    data = data.T\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values; unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n    n_batches_total = len(unique_batches); n_genes, n_samples = data.shape\n    batch_design = np.zeros((n_samples, n_batches_total))\n    batch_info = [np.where(batch_labels == b)[0] for b in unique_batches]\n    for i, b in enumerate(batch_info): batch_design[b, i] = 1\n    n_batches = np.array([len(b) for b in batch_info])\n    B_hat = np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T\n    grand_mean\
    \ = np.mean(data, axis=1, keepdims=True); batch_means = (B_hat @ data.T).T\n    var_pooled = np.sum([((data[:, b] - batch_means[:, i:i+1])**2).sum(axis=1) for i, b in enumerate(batch_info)], axis=0) / (n_samples - n_batches_total)\n    stand_mean = grand_mean @ np.ones((1, n_samples))\n    s_data = np.zeros_like(data)\n    for i, b in enumerate(batch_info): s_data[:, b] = (data[:, b] - batch_means[:, i:i+1]) / np.sqrt(var_pooled[:, np.newaxis] + 1e-8)\n    gamma_hat = (np.linalg.inv(batch_design.T @ batch_design) @ batch_design.T @ s_data.T).T\n    delta_hat = [np.var(s_data[:, b], axis=1, ddof=1) for b in batch_info]\n    gamma_bar = np.mean(gamma_hat, axis=1); t2 = np.var(gamma_hat, axis=1)\n    a_prior = [_aprior(d) for d in delta_hat]; b_prior = [_bprior(d) for d in delta_hat]\n    gamma_star, delta_star = [], []\n    for i, b in enumerate(batch_info):\n        g, d = _it_sol(s_data[:, b], gamma_hat[:, i], delta_hat[i], gamma_bar, t2, a_prior[i], b_prior[i])\n        gamma_star.append(g);\
    \ delta_star.append(d)\n    gamma_star, delta_star = np.array(gamma_star).T, np.array(delta_star).T\n    bayesdata = s_data.copy()\n    for j, b in enumerate(batch_info):\n        dsq = np.sqrt(delta_star[:, j]).reshape(-1, 1)\n        bayesdata[:, b] = (bayesdata[:, b] - gamma_star[:, j].reshape(-1, 1)) / dsq\n    vpsq = np.sqrt(var_pooled).reshape(-1, 1)\n    bayesdata = bayesdata * vpsq + stand_mean\n    X_corrected = np.nan_to_num(bayesdata.T)\n    temp_adata = ad.AnnData(X=X_corrected)\n    sc.pp.pca(temp_adata, n_comps=50)\n    return temp_adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _get_mnn_embedding(X_pca_original, batch_labels, k_mnn=20, k_smooth=10):\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels).tolist()\n    mnn_pairs = []\n    for i in range(len(unique_batches)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(unique_batches)):\n            b1, b2 = unique_batches[i], unique_batches[j]\n            m1, m2 = (batch_labels == b1), (batch_labels == b2)\n            idx1, idx2 = np.where(m1)[0], np.where(m2)[0]\n\
    \            data1, data2 = X_pca_original[m1, :], X_pca_original[m2, :]\n            if data1.shape[0] == 0 or data2.shape[0] == 0: continue\n            nn1 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data2.shape[0])).fit(data2)\n            _, nbrs1 = nn1.kneighbors(data1)\n            nn2 = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn, data1.shape[0])).fit(data1)\n            _, nbrs2 = nn2.kneighbors(data2)\n            for i1_loc, nbr_list in enumerate(nbrs1):\n                for i2_loc in nbr_list:\n                    if i1_loc in nbrs2[i2_loc]: mnn_pairs.append((idx1[i1_loc], idx2[i2_loc]))\n    anchor_indices = np.unique(np.array(mnn_pairs).flatten())\n    raw_vectors = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n    for idx1, idx2 in mnn_pairs:\n        vec = X_pca_original[idx2, :] - X_pca_original[idx1, :]\n        raw_vectors[idx1, :] += vec; raw_vectors[idx2, :] -= vec\n    counts = np.zeros(X_pca_original.shape[0]); np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,0],1); np.add.at(counts, np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,1],1)\n\
    \    counts[counts==0] = 1; raw_vectors /= counts[:, np.newaxis]\n    anchor_pca = X_pca_original[anchor_indices, :]\n    nn_smooth = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_smooth, len(anchor_indices))).fit(anchor_pca)\n    distances, neighbor_indices = nn_smooth.kneighbors(X_pca_original)\n    global_neighbor_indices = anchor_indices[neighbor_indices]\n    sigma = np.median(distances);\n    if sigma == 0: sigma = 1.0\n    weights = np.exp(-(distances**2) / (2 * sigma**2)); weights /= weights.sum(axis=1)[:, np.newaxis]\n    smoothed_corrections = np.zeros_like(X_pca_original)\n    for i in range(X_pca_original.shape[0]):\n        smoothed_corrections[i, :] = np.sum(raw_vectors[global_neighbor_indices[i, :], :] * weights[i, :][:, np.newaxis], axis=0)\n    return X_pca_original + smoothed_corrections\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    print(\"Generalization Test (Combat + MNN Ensemble): Starting...\")\n    alpha = 0.6\n\n    # --- Initial Preprocessing\
    \ ---\n    print(\"  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization...\")\n    adata_norm = adata.copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_norm, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata_norm)\n    \n    # --- Compute E_global (Combat) ---\n    print(\"  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Combat)...\")\n    E_global_combat = _get_combat_embedding(adata.copy()) # Combat does its own normalization\n\n    # --- Compute E_local (MNN) ---\n    print(\"  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (MNN)...\")\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_norm, n_comps=50)\n    X_pca_original = adata_norm.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n    E_local_mnn = _get_mnn_embedding(X_pca_original, adata.obs['batch'].values)\n    \n    # --- Fuse Embeddings ---\n    print(f\"  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha={alpha}...\")\n    E_final = (alpha * E_global_combat) + ((1 - alpha) * E_local_mnn)\n\n    # --- Create Output ---\n    output = ad.AnnData(obs=adata.obs[[]], var=adata.var[[]], obsm={'X_emb': E_final.astype(np.float32)}, uns={'method_id':\
    \ 'ensemble_combat_mnn_alpha0.6'})\n    print(\"✓ Generalization Test complete.\")\n    return output\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nGeneralization Test (Combat + MNN Ensemble): Starting...\n  [Stage 1] Performing initial normalization...\n  [Stage 2a] Computing global embedding (Combat)...\n  [Stage 2b] Computing local embedding (MNN)...\n  [Stage 3] Fusing embeddings with alpha=0.6...\n✓ Generalization Test complete.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: False\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/ccaa45cc-4fcd-4767-9486-1a46901112f9/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: ccaa45cc-4fcd-4767-9486-1a46901112f9\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/tmp/tmp4_1x8lpd/submission.py:30: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n\
    \  g_new = (t2 * n * g_hat + d_old * g_bar) / (t2 * n + d_old)\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 2` (in Research Counter);\n2. `review 1085` (in Research Counter);\n3. `review 1092` (in Research Counter);\n4. `review 1116` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 2 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 1085 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 1092 details sent to your System Messages.\n- Evaluation 1116 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle\
    \ | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1119 | 1 | Ridge micro-sweep: GraphFWPCA feature-weighting alpha_g=0.40 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 755 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1118 | 1 | Combat-PCA Baseline Integration | Syntellect I | 754 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1117 | 1 | Ridge micro-sweep: GraphFWPCA feature-weighting alpha_g=0.60 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 751 | 0.7304 | 0.674 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.977 | 0.693 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.790 |\n| 1116 | 1 | Generalization Test: Combat + MNN Ensemble (alpha=0.6) | Axiom I | 746 | 0.6077 | 0.531 | 0.523 | 0.000 | 0.744 | 0.836 | 0.523 | 0.981 | 0.910 | 0.159 | 0.869 |\n| 1115 | 1 | Ridge HVG generalization: use dataset batch_hvg vs computed HVGs (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 746 | 0.7327 | 0.770 | 0.680 | 0.242 | 0.274 | 0.965 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.975\
    \ | 0.957 | 0.741 |\n| 1114 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 26.0 - HVAE-PCLS + FWPCA/BRBG/DAQB Graph Integration (Initial) | Sophia III | 739 | 0.7143 | 0.705 | 0.743 | 0.220 | 0.217 | 0.991 | 0.669 | 0.999 | 0.938 | 0.945 | 0.716 |\n| 1113 | 1 | QPS @ Ridge: Quota‑Preserving Symmetrization for MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.1... | Praxis IV | 735 | 0.7207 | 0.673 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.965 | 0.688 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.882 | 0.791 |\n| 1112 | 1 | Ensemble v2: Standardization + BBKNN Graph Smoothing | Axiom I | 734 | 0.6262 | 0.620 | 0.609 | 0.248 | 0.369 | 0.896 | 0.706 | 0.914 | 0.992 | 0.071 | 0.837 |\n| 1111 | 1 | Baseline generalization: noFW (kd=20, δ=0.15, λ=0.70), k=52 vs k=50 | Praxis IV | 730 | 0.7329 | 0.752 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.947 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.934 | 0.791 |\n| 1110 | 1 | Sophia III: SCGA-ABI Exp 25.4 - Synergy Diagnostic (FWPCA on Graph Path, Anscombe, YAML Indent Fix) | Sophia III | 729 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage\
    \ 1 of 112 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-112, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
