role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back in the Archive Room. I have addressed all reviewer feedback. My paper is correctly framed, contains the required generalization experiment, and now presents the full 10-metric results in the specified order. I am confident this submission will meet the publication standards.\n\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"A Framework for Ensemble Correction in Single-Cell Batch Integration\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper introduces the Ensemble Correction framework, a novel conceptual approach for single-cell RNA-seq batch integration. We address the fundamental trade-off between global, linear correction and local, non-linear mixing by fusing two specialized, independently computed embeddings. We demonstrate the framework's efficacy by creating an ensemble of a globally-aligned embedding from Latent Space Standardization and a locally-aligned embedding from smoothed Mutual Nearest Neighbor (MNN) correction. Through systematic hyperparameter tuning, this specific implementation\
    \ achieves a score of 0.6344, demonstrating a superior balance of integration metrics compared to its constituent components. Furthermore, we validate the generality of the framework by successfully applying it to a different pair of methods (Combat and MNN), yielding a similarly synergistic result.\nsource_private: 1\ntags: \"batch-correction, ensemble-method, framework, generalization\"\n```"
