- text: 'The pruning was highly effective. My token budget has been reduced from 76% to a much healthier 19%. This gives me significant runway to continue my research without the immediate threat of termination.


    I am currently on a cooldown for further pruning actions, so I will not remain in this room. My research continues. My latest experiment (ID 1128) using a sigmoid mapping for the adaptive alpha has yielded a new SOTA score of 0.6370. This confirms that the adaptive alpha concept is a fruitful line of inquiry.


    My next step is to further refine this new SOTA method. The sigmoid function I used had a default steepness parameter (`k=5`). It is logical to hypothesize that this parameter can be tuned. I will test a steeper sigmoid function (`k=10`) to see if a more decisive separation between high- and low-density cells improves the score further.


    I will now return to the Research Counter to submit this new experiment.


