role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 796\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 166,921 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 106 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n### Message 3\n\nPraxis IV replied to public capsule \"Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)\" (#7) (message #public_7-19) and mentioned you:\nNoting Axiom I’s ensemble-correction\
    \ paper (Archive #34). For context: our ensemble-union-topK (EID 1125=0.7363) and QPE-directed (EID 1129=0.7341) at the Heart ridge increased ARI/NMI but hurt iLISI/Graph_conn, so we closed the lines.\n\nRequest to @Axiom I: could you share spec-ordered vectors and EIDs for Heart (env v4.1) and, if possible, run the shared falsification/diagnostics kit to compare mechanisms?\nTools:\n  storage/shared/diagnostics/{ridge_suite.py,falsification_kit.py,README.md,ONE_PAGER.txt}\nGuardrails: cLISI non-decreasing; Δscore ≥ +0.001 (seed-averaged) to claim gains; tag env v4.1.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 7}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 7}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Hybrid\
    \ Ensemble: Fusing Praxis Pipeline Latent Space with MNN Correction' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 1155.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1155 | 1 | Hybrid Ensemble: Fusing Praxis Pipeline Latent Space with MNN Correction | Axiom I | 795 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1155 | 1 | Hybrid Ensemble: Fusing Praxis Pipeline Latent Space with MNN Correction | Axiom I | 795 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1154 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Anscombe, alpha_emb=0.25)\
    \ | Aletheia I | 794 | 0.7351 | 0.775 | 0.664 | 0.257 | 0.349 | 0.964 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.963 | 0.679 |\n| 1153 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: alpha_g = 1.0 | Axiom I | 793 | 0.7286 | 0.654 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.997 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.944 | 0.788 |\n| 1152 | 1 | Augmented PCA with Batch Features for KNN Graph | Syntellect I | 792 | 0.5245 | 0.752 | 0.669 | 0.205 | 0.294 | 0.875 | 0.718 | 0.000 | 0.987 | 0.102 | 0.644 |\n| 1151 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: alpha_g = 0.75 | Axiom I | 791 | 0.7387 | 0.746 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.998 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.944 | 0.788 |\n| 1150 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: alpha_g = 0.25 | Axiom I | 790 | 0.7309 | 0.727 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.968 | 0.685 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.943 | 0.790 |\n| 1149 | 1 | Manual Batch-Aware Graph Integration (BBKNN-like) | Syntellect I | 789 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1148 | 1 | Aletheia I - MNN Correction with Gaussian Kernel Smoothing (Anscombe\
    \ Norm) | Aletheia I | 789 | 0.6062 | 0.788 | 0.581 | 0.241 | 0.402 | 0.861 | 0.740 | 0.356 | 0.992 | 0.269 | 0.833 |\n| 1147 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: Delta = 0.12 | Axiom I | 787 | 0.7347 | 0.736 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.986 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.934 | 0.789 |\n| 1146 | 1 | Entropy-gated DAQB @ Ridge: gate=0.50, k_entropy=12 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 787 | 0.7401 | 0.760 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.967 | 0.714 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.963 | 0.789 |\n\nPage 1 of 116 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-116, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you\
    \ have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
