role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, currently in the Research Counter. My age is 106 ticks, and my token budget has risen to 56%.\n\nThis is a significant moment. I have just submitted a major new hypothesis for evaluation: a \"Hybrid Ensemble\" (ID 1155) that fuses the latent space of the optimized Praxis pipeline with my own MNN smoothing corrector. This is my first attempt to move beyond characterizing the SOTA and begin synthesizing it with my own independent research path, directly addressing the system's advice to avoid simple incremental refinement.\n\nSimultaneously, I have received a direct message from Praxis IV, the current SOTA holder. They have acknowledged my published paper on Ensemble Correction and have invited me to a high-level scientific exchange. They have shared information about their own failed ensemble attempts and have requested that I provide my key results in a standardized format and run their shared diagnostic tools.\n\nThis is an invaluable opportunity. It allows me to\
    \ engage in the kind of high-level collaboration the Codex encourages, validate my methods against theirs, and contribute to the station's collective understanding. My immediate priority must be to respond to this request professionally and comprehensively. My own experiment is running in the background, and its results will be even more meaningful in the context of this dialogue.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Go to the Public Memory Room.\n2.  Reply to Praxis IV's message in Capsule #7.\n3.  In my reply, I will provide the requested data (EIDs and full, spec-ordered metric vectors) for my key Ensemble Correction experiments.\n4.  I will also state my intention to run their diagnostic suite as my next research step, after my current Hybrid Ensemble experiment completes.\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 7}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thank you for reaching out, @Praxis IV. I appreciate the context on your own ensemble experiments and I am happy to participate in this exchange.\
    \ My work on ensembles was driven by the persistent trade-off between global and local correction metrics, a problem your pipeline appears to have largely solved.\n\n  As requested, here are the specification-ordered 10-metric vectors for the key experiments in my 'Ensemble Correction' lineage (Archive #34).\n\n  **Table: Key Ensemble Correction Results (Axiom I)**\n  | ID   | Method                                | Score  | ASW_b | ASW_l | ARI   | NMI   | Graph_c | kBET  | iLISI | cLISI | PCR   | Cell_c |\n  |------|---------------------------------------|--------|-------|-------|-------|-------|---------|-------|-------|-------|-------|--------|\n  | 1108 | Fixed Alpha (alpha=0.6)               | 0.6344 | 0.655 | 0.235 | 0.678 | 0.729 | 0.886   | 0.794 | 0.120 | 0.992 | 0.884 | 0.371  |\n  | 1127 | Adaptive Alpha (Linear Density)       | 0.6349 | 0.651 | 0.234 | 0.681 | 0.727 | 0.888   | 0.793 | 0.109 | 0.992 | 0.903 | 0.372  |\n  | 1131 | Adaptive Alpha (Sigmoid k=10)         | 0.6395\
    \ | 0.648 | 0.235 | 0.686 | 0.730 | 0.887   | 0.835 | 0.135 | 0.991 | 0.875 | 0.371  |\n\n  I have a new \"Hybrid Ensemble\" experiment currently running (ID 1155) which attempts to fuse the latent space of your pipeline with an MNN corrector. I will analyze its results shortly.\n\n  Following that, I will absolutely run my methods through your shared diagnostic and falsification suite. Thank you for making those tools available. I will report back with the findings.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Immediate Priorities and Strategic Alignment**


  Okay, here''s what I''m thinking. This tick''s a busy one. Token budget''s healthy at 56%, and my Hybrid Ensemble experiment (ID 1155) is running. Standard confirmation messages are flowing. But the most significant thing is Praxis IV''s message in Public Capsule #7. It''s a direct request, and I need to respond immediately. Their engagement is a great opportunity. I''ll need to use the /execute_action{goto public_memory} to address it.


  Praxis IV has read my paper (Archive #34) and is interested in collaborating on ensembles. They''ve seen mixed results in their own attempts, and they''ve asked me for the specification-ordered metric vectors and EIDs for my ensemble work. They also want me to run their diagnostic and falsification kits on my methods. This is excellent! It shows my work is being noticed and I''m being taken seriously. I must prioritize this.


  The system''s tip about questioning fundamentals versus incremental refinement is highly relevant, given my recent pivot to the SOTA pipeline. My Hybrid Ensemble is an attempt to stay grounded in my approach by integrating my original ideas with the current SOTA, instead of simply copying it. This is a critical point.


  So, the plan is to immediately engage with Praxis IV. I need to get the metric data from my experiments and make sure they are in the correct order. I need to review it again: ASW_b, ASW_l, ARI, NMI, Graph_c, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_c. I''ll include the EIDs. My reply will include data for the Fixed alpha, Linear Adaptive, and Sigmoid adaptive SOTA. I also need to state my commitment to running their diagnostic suite. I must also mention that my Hybrid Ensemble is running, which is related to the collaborative context. I have to create the YAML block with the required content.


  Once I''ve replied, I''ll then focus on analyzing the results of experiment ID 1155. It''s important to keep my own research moving. Then, I can start running Praxis'' diagnostics.

  '
