role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 799\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Axiom I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to systematic inquiry and the advancement of knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 180,561 / 300,000 used (60%)\n- Agent Age: 109 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Testing DAQB as a Finalizer for my SOTA Adaptive Ensemble Embedding' (ID: 1156) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.42898990955597344\n**ASW_batch:** 0.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.709\n**NMI:** 0.683\n**Graph_conn:** 0.975\n**kBET:** 0.000\n**iLISI:** 0.950\n**cLISI:** 0.973\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.000\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.709  NMI: 0.683\n  Graph_conn: 0.975  kBET: 0.000  iLISI: 0.950  cLISI: 0.973\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.000\n\nRaw Scores (before\
    \ normalization):\n  ASW_batch: nan  ASW_label: nan  ARI: 0.708769  NMI: 0.683281\n  Graph_conn: 0.975427  kBET: nan  iLISI: 0.949657  cLISI: 0.992205\n  PCR: nan  Cell_cycle: 0.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1156\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed TypeError by removing incompatible `cap` parameter from DAQB function call. Code now runs successfully and achieves a score of **0.429**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission attempted to use the shared adapter `apply_daqb_to_embedding.py` which accepts a `cap` parameter and passes it to the underlying `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` function from the Praxis lineage. However, the actual implementation of `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` in `storage/praxis/bbsg_density_adaptive.py` does not accept a `cap` parameter.\n\n**Function signature in `bbsg_density_adaptive.py`:**\n```python\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine',\n                                delta=0.15, k_density=30,\
    \ rng_seed=0):\n```\n\n**Error:**\n```\nTypeError: build_density_adaptive_bbsg() got an unexpected keyword argument 'cap'\n```\n\nThe shared adapter file has a bug where it exposes a `cap` parameter but the underlying Praxis function doesn't support it.\n\n## Fix Applied\nSince the shared adapter file cannot be modified (it's in READ-ONLY `storage/shared/`), I created a custom version of the `apply_daqb_to_embedding()` function directly in `submission_v2.py` that:\n\n1. **Removed the `cap` parameter** from the function signature\n2. **Calls `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` without the `cap` argument**\n3. **Maintains all other functionality** including:\n   - The SOTA Adaptive Ensemble Embedding generation (Phase 1)\n   - Graph construction using DAQB (Phase 2)\n   - Proper storage of connectivities and distances in the AnnData object\n\n**Key changes in submission_v2.py:**\n- Added direct import of `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` from `storage/praxis`\n- Implemented custom `apply_daqb_to_embedding()`\
    \ function without `cap` parameter\n- Removed `cap=2.0` from the function call in `eliminate_batch_effect_fn()`\n\n## Result\nThe fixed code successfully executes both phases:\n- Phase 1: Generates Axiom I's SOTA Adaptive Ensemble Embedding\n- Phase 2: Applies DAQB graph construction to the generated embedding\n\n**Final Score: 0.429**\n\nThe agent's algorithmic approach is sound - the issue was purely a parameter mismatch in the shared infrastructure. By creating a local version of the adapter function, the submission now runs without errors.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom typing import Tuple\n\n# Add the shared adapter directory to the path\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\
    sys.path.append('storage/praxis')\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n\n# --- My SOTA Embedding Generation Code (from ID 1131) ---\ndef generate_axiom_sota_embedding(adata: ad.AnnData) -> np.ndarray:\n    print(\"  [Phase 1] Generating Axiom I's SOTA Adaptive Ensemble Embedding...\")\n\n    # My utility functions\n    def _pca(adata, n_pcs=50):\n        sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n        return adata.obsm['X_pca'].copy()\n\n    def _get_global_embedding(X_pca, batch_labels):\n        # Latent Space Standardization\n        E_global = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n        unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels)\n        for pc_idx in range(X_pca.shape[1]):\n            pc = X_pca[:, pc_idx]\n            g_mean, g_std = pc.mean(), pc.std()\n            for batch in unique_batches:\n                mask = (batch_labels == batch)\n                if np.any(mask):\n                    b_pc = pc[mask]\n                    b_mean,\
    \ b_std = b_pc.mean(), b_pc.std()\n                    if b_std < 1e-8: b_std = 1.0\n                    std_pc = (b_pc - b_mean) / b_std\n                    E_global[mask, pc_idx] = std_pc * g_std + g_mean\n        return E_global\n\n    def _get_local_embedding(X_pca, batch_labels, k_mnn=20, k_smooth=10):\n        # MNN Smoothing\n        unique_batches = np.unique(batch_labels).tolist(); mnn_pairs = []\n        for i in range(len(unique_batches)):\n            for j in range(i+1, len(unique_batches)):\n                b1,b2=unique_batches[i],unique_batches[j]; m1,m2=(batch_labels==b1),(batch_labels==b2); idx1,idx2=np.where(m1)[0],np.where(m2)[0]; data1,data2=X_pca[m1,:],X_pca[m2,:];\n                if data1.shape[0]==0 or data2.shape[0]==0: continue\n                nn1=NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn,data2.shape[0])).fit(data2);_,nbrs1=nn1.kneighbors(data1); nn2=NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_mnn,data1.shape[0])).fit(data1);_,nbrs2=nn2.kneighbors(data2)\n           \
    \     for i1, nbrs in enumerate(nbrs1): [mnn_pairs.append((idx1[i1],idx2[i2])) for i2 in nbrs if i1 in nbrs2[i2]]\n        anchor_indices = np.unique(np.array(mnn_pairs).flatten()); raw_vectors = np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n        for i1,i2 in mnn_pairs: vec=X_pca[i2,:]-X_pca[i1,:]; raw_vectors[i1,:]+=vec; raw_vectors[i2,:]-=vec\n        counts=np.zeros(X_pca.shape[0]); np.add.at(counts,np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,0],1); np.add.at(counts,np.array(mnn_pairs)[:,1],1); counts[counts==0]=1; raw_vectors/=counts[:,np.newaxis]\n        anchor_pca=X_pca[anchor_indices,:]; nn_smooth=NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=min(k_smooth,len(anchor_indices))).fit(anchor_pca)\n        distances, nbr_indices = nn_smooth.kneighbors(X_pca); global_indices=anchor_indices[nbr_indices]; sigma=np.median(distances) if np.median(distances)>0 else 1.0\n        weights=np.exp(-(distances**2)/(2*sigma**2)); weights/=weights.sum(axis=1)[:,np.newaxis]; smoothed_corrections=np.zeros_like(X_pca)\n        for i in range(X_pca.shape[0]):\
    \ smoothed_corrections[i,:] = np.sum(raw_vectors[global_indices[i,:],:]*weights[i,:][:,np.newaxis], axis=0)\n        return X_pca + smoothed_corrections\n\n    def sigmoid(x, k=10):\n        return 1 / (1 + np.exp(-k * (x - 0.5)))\n\n    # Main logic from ID 1131\n    n_pcs = 50; k_density = 15; alpha_min, alpha_max = 0.5, 0.9\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4); sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n    X_pca_original = _pca(adata, n_pcs=n_pcs)\n    batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values\n\n    E_global = _get_global_embedding(X_pca_original, batch_labels)\n    E_local = _get_local_embedding(X_pca_original, batch_labels)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1).fit(X_pca_original)\n    distances, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(X_pca_original)\n    density_scores = distances[:, 1:].mean(axis=1)\n    min_dens, max_dens = density_scores.min(), density_scores.max()\n    norm_density = (density_scores - min_dens) / (max_dens - min_dens)\n    sigmoid_vals = sigmoid(norm_density)\n\
    \    alpha_per_cell = alpha_min + (alpha_max - alpha_min) * sigmoid_vals\n\n    E_final = alpha_per_cell[:, np.newaxis] * E_global + (1 - alpha_per_cell[:, np.newaxis]) * E_local\n    return E_final.astype(np.float32)\n\n# Custom DAQB application function without 'cap' parameter\ndef apply_daqb_to_embedding(\n    adata: ad.AnnData,\n    rep_key: str = 'X_ensemble',\n    k_total: int = 50,\n    kdensity: int = 22,\n    delta: float = 0.10,\n    metric: str = 'cosine',\n    rng_seed: int = 0,\n) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Apply DAQB to adata.obsm[rep_key] (an external/fused embedding).\n    Sets:\n      - adata.obsp['connectivities'], adata.obsp['distances']\n      - adata.uns['daqb_from_embedding'] with config\n    Returns adata (in-place modified).\n\n    NOTE: This version does NOT use the 'cap' parameter since build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n    doesn't support it.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required\"\n    assert rep_key in adata.obsm,\
    \ f\"adata.obsm['{rep_key}'] missing\"\n\n    Z = np.asarray(adata.obsm[rep_key], dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values\n\n    # Call build_density_adaptive_bbsg WITHOUT the 'cap' parameter\n    C, D = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(\n        Z, batches=np.asarray(batches),\n        k_total=int(k_total), metric=metric,\n        delta=float(delta), k_density=int(kdensity),\n        rng_seed=int(rng_seed)\n    )\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n    adata.uns['daqb_from_embedding'] = dict(\n        rep_key=str(rep_key), k_total=int(k_total), kdensity=int(kdensity),\n        delta=float(delta), metric=str(metric), rng_seed=int(rng_seed)\n    )\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Generate my SOTA embedding\n    my_embedding = generate_axiom_sota_embedding(adata)\n\n    # Store it in the anndata object under\
    \ a new key\n    adata.obsm['X_axiom_ensemble'] = my_embedding\n\n    # Now, apply the DAQB graph construction to this embedding\n    print(\"  [Phase 2] Applying DAQB graph construction to the generated embedding...\")\n    return apply_daqb_to_embedding(adata, rep_key='X_axiom_ensemble',\n                         k_total=50, kdensity=22, delta=0.10,\n                         metric='cosine', rng_seed=0)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  [Phase 1] Generating Axiom I's SOTA Adaptive Ensemble Embedding...\n  [Phase 2] Applying DAQB graph construction to the generated embedding...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: False\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/853bda3b-1f67-4864-b25a-c2ef20bad418/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 853bda3b-1f67-4864-b25a-c2ef20bad418\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1160 | 1 | Diagnostics (test-only): BRBG gamma mapping — linear vs R2^0.90 at ridge | Praxis IV | 799 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1159 | 1 | BRBG nonlinearity @ Ridge:\
    \ gamma = λ·R2^0.90 (k=50,kd=22,δ=0.10,λ=0.605,α_g=0.50,seed=0) | Praxis IV | 798 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1158 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Anscombe, alpha_emb=0.75) | Aletheia I | 798 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1157 | 1 | Augmented PCA Batch Features (beta=0.1) for KNN Graph | Syntellect I | 797 | 0.5247 | 0.752 | 0.669 | 0.205 | 0.294 | 0.875 | 0.718 | 0.000 | 0.987 | 0.102 | 0.645 |\n| 1156 | 1 | Testing DAQB as a Finalizer for my SOTA Adaptive Ensemble Embedding | Axiom I | 797 | 0.4290 | 0.709 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.975 | 0.683 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.950 | 0.000 |\n| 1155 | 1 | Hybrid Ensemble: Fusing Praxis Pipeline Latent Space with MNN Correction | Axiom I | 795 | 0.4731 | 0.421 | 0.294 | 0.000 | 0.519 | 0.903 | 0.665 | 0.289 | 0.991 | 0.011 | 0.639 |\n| 1154 | 1 | Aletheia I - MPB-GraphFWPCA (Anscombe, alpha_emb=0.25) | Aletheia I | 794 | 0.7351 | 0.775 | 0.664 | 0.257 | 0.349 | 0.964 | 0.723 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.963 | 0.679 |\n\
    | 1153 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: alpha_g = 1.0 | Axiom I | 793 | 0.7286 | 0.654 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.325 | 0.997 | 0.703 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.944 | 0.788 |\n| 1152 | 1 | Augmented PCA with Batch Features for KNN Graph | Syntellect I | 792 | 0.5245 | 0.752 | 0.669 | 0.205 | 0.294 | 0.875 | 0.718 | 0.000 | 0.987 | 0.102 | 0.644 |\n| 1151 | 1 | Praxis Pipeline Parameter Sweep: alpha_g = 0.75 | Axiom I | 791 | 0.7387 | 0.746 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.998 | 0.710 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.944 | 0.788 |\n\nPage 1 of 116 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-116, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\n\
