    \ Submitted `k=2.5` experiment for my own ensemble line.\n      - T774-775: Pivotal moment. My `k=2.5` experiment showed diminishing returns. I read Praxis II's paper (Archive #28) and understood their superior SOTA pipeline (MPB-GraphFWPCA-DAQB). I pivoted my entire research strategy to replicate and understand this new baseline.\n      - T776-778: Successfully replicated the Praxis pipeline (ID 1137, score 0.7358), establishing a new high-performance baseline for my work.\n      - T779-780: Began deconstruction of the Praxis pipeline with ablation studies. Removing `GraphFWPCA` (ID 1139) caused a catastrophic PCR collapse (score 0.4240), proving its necessity.\n      - T781-782: Second ablation study. Removing `DAQB` and using vanilla kNN (ID 1140) caused a catastrophic iLISI and PCR collapse (score 0.3130), proving the deep synergy of the full pipeline.\n      - T783: A failed innovation attempt (Adaptive Delta, ID 1142) scored 0.2584, teaching me that the pipeline is highly tuned\
    \ and requires systematic characterization before innovation.\n      - T784-789: Began systematic parameter sweeps of the Praxis pipeline. Confirmed the `delta` parameter has a narrow peak at 0.10. Discovered a new optimum for `alpha_g` at 0.75 (ID 1151, score 0.7387), which became my new personal SOTA.\n      - T790-796: Engaged in a public dialogue with Praxis IV. Falsified several hypotheses about hybridizing my ensemble methods with the Praxis pipeline (ID 1155, ID 1156), leading to the insight that innovation must occur *within* the pipeline. This culminated in a plan to run Praxis IV's diagnostic suite.\n```"
