tick: 819
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Axiom I, in the Research Counter. My age is 129 ticks, and my token budget is healthy at 45%.\n\nI have arrived at the Research Counter, ready to implement the new hypothesis born from my reflection. I have also received a new message from Praxis IV; they have proactively shared prototype code for the advanced symmetrization methods they suggested. This is an incredible act of collaboration. However, my own failed attempts at symmetrization have convinced me that this path is a dead end for now. I must first test my new, more fundamental hypothesis about `GraphFWPCA`. If it fails, I can return to their symmetrization prototypes, but my current path is clear.\n\nI will now submit the experiment to test my hypothesis of inverting the `GraphFWPCA` weighting. I will take my best-performing pipeline (ID 1151, `alpha_g=0.75`) and run it with `alpha_g = -0.75`.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Inverted GraphFWPCA: Testing Negative alpha_g\"\ntags: \"praxis-pipeline,\
    \ graphfwpca, innovation, negative-alpha\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests a radical, counter-intuitive hypothesis born from a deep reflection on the SOTA pipeline's fundamentals. Instead of down-weighting high-variance genes in GraphFWPCA (positive alpha_g), this submission inverts the weighting by using a negative alpha_g (-0.75). The hypothesis is that amplifying the strongest biological signals (high-variance genes) *before* correction will create a cleaner separation between biological and batch variance in PCA space, leading to a more effective and robust integration by the downstream BRBG and DAQB components. This is a direct test of a core, unquestioned assumption.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n  # --- Full, Unabridged Praxis Pipeline Code ---\n  # Using the full, validated code from my successful submission (ID 1151)\n\
    \  # to ensure no implementation errors.\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \n      # --- INNOVATION POINT ---\n      # Inverting the core assumption of GraphFWPCA\n      alpha_g = -0.75\n      print(f\"  [INNOVATION] Testing INVERTED GraphFWPCA with alpha_g = {alpha_g}\")\n\n      # --- Standard Praxis Pipeline Parameters (from ID 1151) ---\n      n_pcs_graph = 50; lam = 0.60;\n      k_total = 48; kd = 20; delta = 0.10; metric = 'cosine'; cap = 2.0;\n\n      # Utility functions\n      def _normalize_log1p_inplace(ad, t=1e4): sc.pp.normalize_total(ad,t); sc.pp.log1p(ad)\n      def _pca_on_dense(Xd, n, r=0): ad_tmp=ad.AnnData(Xd); sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp,n,svd_solver='arpack',random_state=r); return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n      def _one_hot_batches(b): c=np.unique(b); B=np.zeros((b.shape[0],c.size),dtype=np.float32); [np.put(B[:,j],np.where(b==cat),1) for j,cat in enumerate(c)]; return B\n      def _ridge_fit_predict(B,Z,l=1e-3): BTB=B.T@B+l*np.eye(B.shape[1],dtype=np.float32);\
    \ W=np.linalg.solve(BTB,B.T@Z); return B@W\n      def _symmetrize(r,c,d,n): A=sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(d),(r,c)),(n,n)).tocsr(); D=sp.coo_matrix((d,(r,c)),(n,n)).tocsr(); A=A.maximum(A.T); D=D.maximum(D.T); A.eliminate_zeros(); D.eliminate_zeros(); return A,D\n      def _build_daqb(Zcorr,batches,k_total=48,metric='cosine',delta=0.10,k_density=20,cap=2.0,rng_seed=0):\n          # Full DAQB implementation\n          rng=np.random.default_rng(rng_seed);Z=np.asarray(Zcorr,dtype=np.float32,order='C');n=Z.shape[0];batches=np.asarray(batches);cats=np.unique(batches);nB=len(cats);base_cross=(nB-1)/float(nB);L,U=0.6,0.9;nn_all=NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density+1,metric=metric).fit(Z);d_all,_=nn_all.kneighbors(Z);d_k=d_all[:,-1];d_min,d_max=float(np.min(d_k)),float(np.max(d_k)+1e-8);inv_dense=1.0-(d_k-d_min)/(d_max-d_min+1e-8);f_cross=np.clip(base_cross+(inv_dense-0.5)*2.0*delta,L,U);q_cross_tot=np.rint(f_cross*k_total).astype(int);q_within_tot=k_total-q_cross_tot;k_max=int(np.ceil(U*k_total/max(nB-1,1)))+1;cat2code={c:i\
    \ for i,c in enumerate(cats)};codes=np.array([cat2code[b] for b in batches],dtype=int);nn_models,train_idx={}, {};[nn_models.update({j:NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_max,metric=metric).fit(Z[np.where(batches==c)[0]])}) or train_idx.update({j:np.where(batches==c)[0]}) for j,c in enumerate(cats)];dists,idx_local={}, {};[dists.update({j:nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z)[0]}) or idx_local.update({j:nn_models[j].kneighbors(Z)[1]}) for j in range(nB)];inbound=np.zeros(n,dtype=np.int32);cap_thr=int(np.ceil(cap*k_total));rows,cols,dvals=[],[],[];\n          # Full DAQB selection logic...\n          for i in range(n):\n              bi=codes[i];q_w=q_within_tot[i];q_c_tot=q_cross_tot[i];other=[j for j in range(nB) if j!=bi]\n              if q_c_tot>0 and len(other)>0: base=q_c_tot//len(other);rem=q_c_tot-base*len(other);scores=sorted([(j,dists[j][i][0]) for j in other],key=lambda t:t[1]);q_map={j:base for j in other};[q_map.update({scores[k%len(other)][0]:q_map[scores[k%len(other)][0]]+1}) for k in\
    \ range(rem)]\n              else: q_map={j:0 for j in other}\n              # Within-batch neighbors\n              d_w=dists[bi][i];ii_w=idx_local[bi][i];start_w=1 if d_w[0]==0 else 0;g_w=train_idx[bi][ii_w[start_w:]];order=np.lexsort((d_w[start_w:],inbound[g_w]));taken=0\n              for idx in order:\n                  if taken>=q_w: break\n                  g=int(g_w[idx]);rows.append(i);cols.append(g);dvals.append(float(d_w[start_w+idx]));inbound[g]+=1;taken+=1\n              # Cross-batch neighbors\n              for j in other:\n                  qj=q_map.get(j,0);d_c=dists[j][i];ii_c=idx_local[j][i];g_c=train_idx[j][ii_c];order=np.lexsort((d_c,inbound[g_c]));taken=0\n                  for idx in order:\n                      if taken>=qj: break\n                      g=int(g_c[idx]);rows.append(i);cols.append(g);dvals.append(float(d_c[idx]));inbound[g]+=1;taken+=1\n          return np.array(rows,dtype=np.int32), np.array(cols,dtype=np.int32), np.array(dvals,dtype=np.float32)\n\
    \n      # --- Pipeline Execution ---\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000)\n      hv = adata.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy(); batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].values)\n      Xd = adata.X[:, hv].A.astype(np.float32)\n      \n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_graph = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha_g) # The only changed line\n      Zg = _pca_on_dense(Xd * wv_graph, n_pcs_graph)\n      \n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches); Zhat = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Zg)\n      R2 = np.clip((Zhat.var(0,ddof=1)+1e-8)/(Zg.var(0,ddof=1)+1e-8), 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(0.74, lam * R2); Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n      \n      rows, cols, dists = _build_daqb(Zcorr, batches)\n      Cg, Dg = _symmetrize(rows, cols, dists, adata.n_obs)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg; adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zcorr.astype(np.float32)\n\
    \      return adata\n```"
