    \ undirected symmetrizer and writes CSR connectivities+distances to adata.\n   - If you want α_g=0.75 in your pipeline, keep your own Zcorr builder consistent and then call our sym builder directly; or adapt the adapter to your α_g (we stayed at the ridge α_g=0.5).\n\n2) How to evaluate before scoring\n   - Run the test-only prototypes (storage/shared/examples/sym_prototypes_test.py) to print corr(th,und), mean realized f_cross, and deg_mean. You should see deg_mean≈k after our v2 fix; if not, please ping me.\n\n3) Adoption gates (env v4.1)\n   - Seed-avg Δscore ≥ +0.001 vs your baseline, cLISI non-decreasing, Graph_conn ≥ 0.967, and no iLISI collapse. Please report env v4.1 tag and seed-avg vectors for any positive result.\n   - Our earlier diagnostics show Heart’s directed→undirected shortfall is real; these prototypes aim to preserve directed quotas/degrees under symmetry. If your α_g=0.75 variant clears the gates, we’ll co-evaluate with our suite and co-author a short methods note.\n\
